UPDATE companies SET description='EMS Solutions operates from Ogden, Utah, along the Wasatch Front near Salt Lake City. The company was founded in 2000 as a contract manufacturer with limited capabilities and now operates as a division of PCB Solutions Inc. Over two decades it has grown into a regional full-service electronic manufacturing services provider.

The facility runs four SMT lines backed by automated optical inspection and automated through-hole placement equipment, supported by solder paste inspection. Core services span printed circuit board assembly, cable and harness assembly, box build, new product introduction, and full turnkey manufacturing that includes procurement, assembly, and test. The company also offers supply chain management, design collaboration, and expedited manufacturing services, handling volumes from prototype through high-volume production.

Customers come from RF and wireless, medical, industrial, aerospace, military, and consumer product sectors. The company cites experience with leaders in each of these fields, providing both prototype and production-run support for a variety of electronic assemblies.

EMS Solutions emphasizes U.S.-based manufacturing as a differentiator, noting that domestic production eliminates international shipping costs, shortens lead times, and subjects operations to stricter regulatory standards that yield safer, higher-quality products. The company states its values center on superior quality, on-time delivery, customer service, and competitive pricing, with in-house IPC training and 100% AOI, SPI, and functional testing built into every order.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS','IPC Standards']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Solder Paste Inspection (SPI)", "Cable and Harness Assembly", "Box Build Assembly", "Turnkey Manufacturing", "Supply Chain Management", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Test Solutions Development", "Design for Manufacturability Feedback", "Expedited Manufacturing Services"], "industries": ["RF / Wireless", "Medical", "Industrial", "Aerospace", "Military / Defense", "Consumer Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Four SMT lines", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) equipment", "Automated Through-Hole placement equipment", "Solder Paste Inspection (SPI) equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Four SMT lines with automated optical inspection and through-hole placement", "Full turnkey manufacturing including procurement, PCBA, cable, and box build", "Two decades of procurement experience for supply chain management", "In-house IPC-certified training and 100% AOI, SPI, and functional testing", "U.S.-based production eliminating international shipping and reducing lead times"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> / and db", "Headquarters Ogden, Utah -> db and /", "Division of PCB Solutions Inc. -> /", "Four SMT lines with AOI and automated through-hole placement -> /", "Industries: RF, medical, industrial, aerospace, military, consumer -> /", "Services: PCBA, cable assemblies, box build, NPI, turnkey, supply chain, test, design collaboration -> /", "RoHS certification -> db", "IPC standards training, 100% AOI/SPI/testing -> /quality", "Proto to high volume -> /", "U.S.-based manufacturing benefits stated -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ems-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2020, EPD (Electronic Parts Distributors) Company is an independent electronic components distributor based in Denver, Colorado. The firm operates from a corporate office in the city and focuses on supplying original products from major global manufacturers.

The company''s product portfolio includes integrated circuits, diodes, capacitors, transistors, modules, and compass sensors. It maintains a line card of original components and emphasizes fast delivery, quality assurance, and customer-centric service. EPD reports that its core values and services have been recognized by more than 2,000 buyers worldwide.

EPD differentiates itself through a stated commitment to fast response, integrity, and a win-win business strategy. The company cites its broad buyer recognition and adherence to ROHS compliance as markers of its reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Global supplier sourcing", "Line card management", "Component cross-referencing", "Inventory availability checks", "ROHS compliance verification"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fast response to customer needs", "Integrity and win-win business strategy", "Recognized by 2,000+ buyers worldwide", "ROHS-compliant component distribution", "Independent distributor with major global supplier lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> db", "Headquarters in Denver, Colorado -> db and page ''/''", "Independent electronic components distributor -> page ''/''", "Product categories: integrated circuits, diodes, capacitors, transistors, modules, compass sensors -> page ''/''", "More than 2,000 buyers worldwide -> page ''/''", "Operating philosophy: fast response, integrity, win-win strategy -> page ''/''", "ROHS certification -> db", "Emphasis on quality components, fast delivery, great customer service -> page ''/''", "Provides information on models of major global suppliers -> page ''/''", "Line card of original products -> page ''/''"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='epd-electronic-parts-distributors-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Edscha Automotive Michigan operates from Auburn Hills, Michigan, as part of the global Edscha group that traces its origins to 1905. The Michigan site employs approximately 130 people and functions within a network of 25 locations worldwide that supply nearly all major automobile manufacturers.

The company produces automotive body components including hinge systems for doors, hoods, and liftgates, as well as brake pedals, handbrakes, and electric drives for liftgates.

Edscha serves the automotive industry broadly, providing components to almost all automobile manufacturers globally.

Edscha positions itself as a strategic development partner to the international automobile industry, emphasizing innovation in articulation and retention systems for vehicle bodies.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hinge system manufacturing", "Brake pedal production", "Handbrake assembly", "Electric liftgate drive assembly", "Machining of hinges and mounting retainers", "Forging", "Cutting", "Stamping", "Robotic welding", "Assembly"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Sectional steel", "Strip steel", "Forging alloys", "Plastic granules"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global network of 25 production sites", "Energy-efficient machining processes for hinges and retainers", "High automation in hinge and driver-control production", "Strategic development partner for OEMs"], "facts_used": ["Location: Auburn Hills, Michigan -> db", "Founded: 1905 -> db", "Employees: 130 -> db", "Certifications: ISO14001, IATF16949 -> db", "Global sites: 25 locations worldwide -> page /", "Products: hinge systems, brake pedals, handbrakes, electric liftgate drives -> page / (Hengersberg description)", "Processes: machining, forging, cutting, stamping, robotic welding, assembly -> page / (multiple locations)", "Materials: sectional steel, strip steel, forging alloys, plastic granules -> page / (consumption data)", "Industry: automotive OEMs -> page /", "Energy efficiency focus in machining -> db capabilities", "Strategic development partner positioning -> page /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='edscha-automotive-michigan' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electrex Inc operates from Hutchinson, Kansas, where it was founded in 1949.

The company designs and builds wire harnesses, battery cables, and electrical panels. Its production relies on fully automated lines, ultrasonic welding, and lean manufacturing practices, with every harness receiving a 100% electrical continuity test to IPC/WHM-A-620 standards. Electrex runs multiple manufacturing facilities and offers technical re-engineering services to reduce cost and update components.

Electrex serves the turf, recreation, construction, public utilities, and agriculture sectors. Long-standing clients include Excel Industries (Hustler Mowers & Big Dog Mowers), a zero-turn mower manufacturer partnered for over 40 years, and Charles Machine Works (Ditch Witch), an underground construction equipment maker partnered for nearly four decades. Altec, a provider to electric utility and telecommunications markets, is a newer account.

The company describes itself as a values-driven Capital III organization guided by Character, Connection, Competence, and Commitment. It emphasizes worldwide shipping from a central U.S. location, high-run discounts from multiple plants, personalized single-point-of-contact service, and a focus on speed to production through automation and just-in-time capability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire harness design and manufacturing", "Battery cable manufacturing", "Electrical panel manufacturing", "Fully automated production", "Ultrasonic welding", "Lean manufacturing", "100% electrical continuity testing", "IPC/WHM-A-620 compliance", "Product re-engineering and cost reduction", "Technical support and component updates", "Just-in-time production support", "Single-point-of-contact project management"], "industries": ["Turf", "Recreation", "Construction", "Public utilities", "Agriculture"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multiple manufacturing locations enabling high-run discounts and worldwide shipping", "Fully automated production with ultrasonic welding and lean processes", "100% electrical continuity testing on every harness to IPC/WHM-A-620", "Technical service team for product re-engineering and component updates", "Values-driven Capital III culture centered on Character, Connection, Competence, Commitment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Hutchinson, Kansas -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Founded year: 1949 -> db founded_year", "Products: wire harnesses, battery cables, electrical panels -> /about", "Processes: fully automated production, ultrasonic welding, lean manufacturing -> /about", "100% electrical continuity test, IPC/WHM-A-620 standards -> /about", "Multiple manufacturing locations -> /about", "Technical service re-engineering -> /about", "Industries: turf, recreation, construction, public utilities, agriculture -> /about", "Client: Excel Industries (Hustler Mowers & Big Dog Mowers) partnership 40+ years -> /about", "Client: Charles Machine Works (Ditch Witch) partnership nearly 4 decades -> /about", "Client: Altec new client -> /about", "Values: Capital III, Character, Connection, Competence, Commitment -> /about", "Worldwide shipping, central location -> /about", "High run discounts, built-in quality -> /about", "Personalized attention, single point of contact -> /about", "Speed to production, just-in-time -> /about", "Certification: ISO 9001:2015 -> / and db", "Company type: Wire Harness Design/Build Manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electrex-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electro Soft, Inc. (ESI) was founded in 1986 by Jim and Sheila Wallace in Montgomeryville, Pennsylvania, just outside Philadelphia. The company remains family-owned and operated; their daughter Karla Trotman, who started cutting wire by hand as a child, now serves as president and CEO.

ESI builds custom wiring harnesses, cable assemblies, printed circuit boards, cabinet assemblies, and military electronics. The shop runs no-minimum prototypes through large-volume batches, maintains records and drawings for three years, and offers repair, rework, and upgrade services.

The company serves aviation, rail, transit, OEM, and defense customers. A noted partnership includes a 20-year relationship supplying components for autonomous guided vehicles (AGVs), and ESI’s ITAR registration supports defense work. Every engagement includes on-staff engineering support, flexible run sizes, and just-in-time delivery.

ESI positions itself as the “value leader” in electronics contract manufacturing, emphasizing quality and service at competitive prices. The founders’ original focus on linked component product lines, quality, and service remains the stated driver of growth, reinforced by ISO 9001 certification and a commitment to never outsourcing production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','RoHS','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cabinet Assembly", "PCB Assembly (Surface Mount & Wave Soldering)", "Custom Wire Harness Assembly", "Custom Cable Assembly", "Military Electronics Assembly", "Panel Assembly", "Repair, Rework, and Upgrade Services", "Engineering Support", "Just-In-Time Fulfillment", "Batch Manufacturing (Prototype to Large Volume)", "RoHS/Lead-Free Assembly", "ITAR Compliant Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aviation", "Rail", "Transit", "OEM", "Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "No-minimum prototypes to large volume orders", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All assembly performed in-house, never outsourced", "On-staff engineering support included with every project", "No-minimum prototype runs through high-volume production", "Just-in-time delivery with three-year record retention", "Family-owned continuity since 1986"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1986 by Jim and Sheila Wallace -> /about", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Headquarters in Montgomeryville, Pennsylvania -> db", "32 full-time skilled professionals -> /about", "Over 16,000 square feet of office and warehouse space -> /about", "All work done in-house, never outsourced -> /about", "Capabilities: cabinet assembly, PCB assembly, custom wiring harness, custom cable assembly, military electronics -> /capabilities, /about, /", "Industries served: aviation, rail, transit, OEM, defense -> /, /about", "ISO 9001 certified -> /, /about, db", "ITAR registered -> db", "RoHS compliant -> db", "No-minimum prototypes and large orders -> /about, /", "Just-in-time delivery -> /, /about", "Records and drawings maintained for three years -> /about", "Repair, rework, and upgrade services -> db", "Karla Trotman president & CEO since founding -> /about", "20-year AGV component manufacturing partnership -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electro-soft-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Design and Manufacturing (EDM), now operating as Pivot-EDM, Inc., traces its roots to 1979 when Rita Bystrek founded Nebraska Electronics, Inc. in Omaha, Nebraska, as a coil winding and assembly business. By 1989 the company had shifted its focus to printed circuit board assemblies and adopted the Electronic Design and Manufacturing name, adding engineering and design services. A move to a new 50,000-square-foot facility in La Vista, a suburb of Omaha, came in 2004, and in 2017 EDM became part of Pivot International, a global product development and manufacturing network.

The La Vista plant provides 50,000 square feet of ESD-protected, temperature- and humidity-controlled production space with 24/7 security monitoring. EDM offers PCB and electromechanical assembly, rapid-turn prototyping, turnkey and box-build solutions, supply-chain management, global sourcing, RoHS and lead-free conversions, rework and modification, engineering and design, service depot support, and encapsulation and coating. The company handles jobs from a single prototype through full turnkey production with direct fulfillment.

EDM serves customers in medical device manufacturing, evidenced by its ISO 13485:2016 certification, and in equipment for potentially explosive environments, supported by ISO 80079-34:2018.

Founded to bring high-quality electronics manufacturing to the Midwest, EDM emphasizes a climate-controlled, secure facility near major highways, a global footprint through Pivot International, and a commitment to supporting customers from prototype to volume production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ISO 80079-34:2018']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly", "Prototyping", "Rapid Turn Prototyping", "Turnkey Assembly", "Box Build", "Supply Chain Management", "Global Sourcing", "RoHS Conversion", "Pb-free Conversion", "Rework and Modification", "Engineering and Design", "Service Depot", "Encapsulation", "Conformal Coating", "Electromechanical Assembly"], "industries": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Potentially explosive environments"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to full turnkey production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["50,000 sq ft ESD-protected, climate-controlled facility", "24/7 security monitoring and controlled access", "Prototype to full turnkey production with direct fulfillment", "Global sourcing and supply chain management through Pivot International", "RoHS-compliant equipment and processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 by Rita Bystrek as Nebraska Electronics Inc. -> /about", "Became Electronic Design and Manufacturing in 1989 -> /about", "Opened 50,000 sq ft facility in La Vista in 2004 -> /about", "Joined Pivot International in 2017 -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about, /, /services", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /about, /, /services", "ISO 80079-34:2018 certified -> /about", "Facility: 50,000 sq ft ESD protected, temperature/humidity controlled, 24/7 security -> /about, /services", "Services: PCB assembly, prototyping, turnkey, box build, supply chain, global sourcing, RoHS conversion, rework, engineering, design, service depot, encapsulation, coating -> /, /services", "Industries: medical device manufacturing, potentially explosive environments -> /abou