UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Technologies International, Inc. (ETI) operates from Fort Atkinson, Wisconsin, where it was founded in 1958. The company functions as a contract manufacturer of electronic assemblies and a supply chain partner, working in combination with American Cable & Harness (ACH) to serve customers with complex projects.

ETI provides printed circuit board assembly (surface mount, through-hole, and mixed technology), wire and cable harness assembly, and integrated box build solutions. Its capabilities include fine-pitch device placement such as BGAs, micro-BGAs, and LGAs, along with new product introduction (NPI) processes and design-for-manufacturability (DFM) support. Quality inspection uses 3D automated optical inspection, X-ray, and functional testing to IPC-A-610 Class II and III standards. The company states its vertically integrated model has been in place since 1990.

ETI serves medical equipment (respirators, controls for examination tables and dental chairs), aeronautics and aviation (cabin lighting and controls for corporate jets), heavy equipment and machinery (high-density mobile storage systems, gaming systems), HVAC industrial controls (commercial dehumidifiers, heat transfer equipment), industrial control components for food equipment used in restaurants, hospitals, nursing homes, and schools, and agriculture (controls for milking parlors). Case studies reference Spudnik (potato equipment), Bay Tek (gaming), and customers in specialized power supplies and tube & pipe cutting equipment.

The company emphasizes its combined ETI/ACH structure as a single source for PCB assembly, wire harness, and box build, aiming to minimize supply chain complexity. Its NPI process is described as delivering up to 30 percent faster time-to-market versus traditional prototyping, and DFM support targets design risks such as traceability, environmental stresses, and testing requirements. Quick turnaround on quotes and IPC-certified trainers are noted as service commitments.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC-A-610 Class II','IPC-A-610 Class III','RoHS compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (surface mount, through-hole, mixed technology)", "Fine-pitch device placement (BGA, micro-BGA, LGA)", "Wire and cable harness assembly", "Custom cable assemblies", "Box build / integrated assembly", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) support", "3D Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "Functional testing", "IPC-A-610 Class II and III compliance", "RoHS compliant manufacturing", "Leaded manufacturing", "Supply chain management"], "industries": ["Medical equipment", "Aeronautics and aviation", "Heavy equipment and machinery", "HVAC industrial controls", "Industrial control components", "Food equipment", "Agriculture", "Gaming", "Specialized power supplies", "Tube and pipe cutting equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3D AOI (automated optical inspection)", "X-ray inspection system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combined ETI/ACH structure providing single-source PCB assembly, wire harness, and box build", "Vertically integrated electronic contract manufacturing since 1990", "NPI process targeting up to 30% faster time-to-market", "DFM support addressing traceability, environmental stresses, and testing requirements", "IPC-A-610 Class II/III certified inspection with 3D AOI, X-ray, and functional testing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 -> db", "Headquarters Fort Atkinson, Wisconsin -> db", "Combined with American Cable & Harness (ACH) -> /", "PCB assembly, wire/cable harness, box build -> /", "Surface mount, through-hole, mixed technology PCB assembly -> /", "Fine-pitch placement: BGA, micro-BGA, LGA -> /", "NPI process up to 30% faster time-to-market -> /", "DFM support for traceability, environmental stresses, testing -> /", "3D AOI, X-ray, functional testing -> /", "IPC-A-610 Class II and III standards -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "RoHS compliant manufacturing -> /", "Vertically integrated since 1990 -> /", "Medical: respirators, exam table controls, dental chair controls -> /", "Aeronautics: cabin lighting, controls for corporate jets -> /", "Heavy equipment: high-density mobile storage, gaming systems -> /", "HVAC: commercial dehumidifiers, heat transfer equipment -> /", "Industrial controls: food equipment for restaurants, hospitals, nursing homes, schools -> /", "Agriculture: milking parlor controls -> /", "Spudnik case study (potato equipment) -> /", "Bay Tek case study (gaming) -> /", "Specialized power supplies customer -> /", "Tube & pipe cutting equipment customer -> /", "IPC certified trainers -> /", "Quick turnaround on quotes -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electronic-technologies-international-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Elite Biomedical Solutions was founded in 2012 in Cincinnati, Ohio, as a family‑owned and operated business dedicated to supplying healthcare organizations with USA‑made replacement parts for clinical equipment. The company began with a focus on infusion and telemetry assets, aiming to eliminate the worry of substandard components.

Today Elite designs, prototypes, validates, and manufactures OEM‑level replacement parts in‑house, using processes that include heat staking, ultrasonic welding, soldering, UV curing, packaging, and validation testing. Its Cincinnati headquarters houses a dedicated training facility and injection‑molding capabilities, while multiple depot repair sites across the country support a range of infusion pumps and syringe modules from brands such as Becton Dickinson, Baxter, B. Braun, and Alaris. The team comprises biomedical, process, and plastics engineers, quality specialists, and certified biomedical equipment technicians.

Customers span individual biomeds, community hospitals, large health systems, and independent service organizations. Elite’s catalog covers hundreds of specific assemblies—rear cases, pressure sensor boards, door assemblies, and battery doors—for devices including the Alaris 8100, Plum A+, CADD Legacy, and Apex Pro lines.

The company emphasizes a values‑driven model built on integrity, quality, and patient safety, offering a one‑year money‑back guarantee on new parts, same‑day shipping for orders placed before 4 p.m. EST, and an average 30 % cost reduction versus OEM pricing. Elite also runs customized BMET training programs at its Cincinnati facility and has been recognized on the Inc. 5000 list (2017‑2021) and as a Cincinnati Best Workplace (2021).', certifications=ARRAY['GMP','ISO certification','FDA registration']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Heat staking and inserting", "Ultrasonic welding", "Soldering", "Packaging", "Validation testing (IQ/OQ/PQ)", "UV curing", "Design and prototyping", "Injection molding", "Assembly (simple to complex)", "Depot repair services", "Biomedical technician training", "Project planning and design reviews", "Process validation (IQ, OQ, PQ)", "Material selection and customization (engineered resins, flame retardant, fiberglass additives)"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Biomedical equipment", "Hospital infusion systems", "Telemetry monitoring", "Clinical asset management", "Independent service organizations (ISOs)", "Biomedical engineering departments"], "materials": ["Engineered resins", "Flame retardant additives", "Fiberglass additives", "Plastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day fulfillment for orders placed before 4\u202fp.m. EST", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day fulfillment on orders placed before 4\u202fp.m. EST", "One-year money-back guarantee on all new replacement parts", "Average 30\u202f% annual cost savings for customers", "USA\u2011based, family\u2011owned manufacturing with ISO certification and FDA registration", "Customized biomedical technician training programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2012 -> db", "Headquarters in Cincinnati, Ohio -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /about", "ISO certification and FDA registration mentioned -> /", "GMP certification -> db", "Multiple depot repair facilities across US -> /about", "In-house manufacturing: design, prototyping, validation, injection molding, assembly -> /", "Processes: heat staking, ultrasonic welding, soldering, packaging, validation testing, UV curing -> /", "Team includes biomedical engineers, process engineers, plastics engineers, quality specialists, biomedical equipment technicians -> /about", "Replacement parts for brands: Becton Dickinson/CareFusion, Baxter, B. Braun, Hospira, Outlook, Alaris, Plum A+, Horizon, Flo-Gard, MedNet -> /", "Specific parts: rear cases, pressure sensor boards, door assemblies, battery doors for Alaris 8100, Plum A+, CADD Legacy, Apex Pro -> /", "Customers: individual BMETs, smaller hospitals, large health systems, independent service organizations -> /about", "One-year money-back guarantee on new parts -> /about", "Same-day fulfillment before 4pm EST -> /about", "Average 30% savings for customers -> /about", "BMET training programs at Cincinnati facility -> /about", "Inc. 5000 fastest-growing 2017-2021 -> /about", "Manny Award for Top Growth in Manufacturing 2017-2020 -> /about", "Fast 55 Top 55 Fastest Growing Companies in Cincinnati 2021 -> /about", "Best Workplaces in Cincinnati 2021 -> /about", "Values-driven model: integrity, quality, patient safety -> /about", "Fair pricing structure -> /about", "Dynamic tech support for biomedical equipment technicians -> /about", "Engineered resins with customizable color and additives (flame retardant, fiber glass) -> /", "Project Plan, Design Reviews, IQ/OQ/PQ validation -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elite-biomedical-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Engineered Medical Systems, Inc. was founded in 1985 in Indianapolis, Indiana, as a privately held medical device manufacturer. The company later expanded to a second facility in Penang, Malaysia, with both sites holding ISO 13485 certification.

The company designs and manufactures disposable air management devices and electronic medical devices. Its capabilities span product design from concept through prototype and tool building, injection molding and complete assembly, bonding via sonic welding, solvents and adhesives, product testing, and finished-device delivery. Operations occupy more than 100,000 square feet of manufacturing space across the Indianapolis and Penang facilities.

Engineered Medical Systems serves the medical device industry, supplying disposable air management products and electronic medical devices to specialty distributors and international markets in over 70 countries. The company also collaborates with brands such as Pulmodyne for innovative product submissions.

