UPDATE companies SET description='Evertech is based in Cedarburg, Wisconsin. The company was founded in 2022 by Michael Scherer, a biomedical engineering graduate from the University of Wisconsin–Madison. Scherer began his career at Gauthier Biomedical as a product development engineer and production manager before founding Tecovan in 2020, where he developed the Autosight® product line. After acquiring Electro‑Pro, Inc. and its PCB assembly line, he launched Evertech to provide advanced electrical and manufacturing solutions.

Evertech delivers full‑service electronic manufacturing, covering concept, schematic, PCB layout, in‑house assembly, and test. Its Cedarburg facility runs surface‑mount and through‑hole assembly, wave and reflow soldering, 3D printing, and machining, supporting prototype runs with a turnaround of under ten days and production runs in about four weeks. The shop handles projects from low‑volume prototypes to full‑scale production for embedded electronics, wireless IoT devices, and industrial control boards.

The company serves startups, OEMs, and engineering teams across medical device, industrial, and wireless IoT markets. Concrete examples include the Autosight® Asset Tracker for steam autoclave sterilization, which uses cellular and Bluetooth technology, and the Autosight® AC Controller that integrates with legacy HVAC systems via Wi‑Fi and Bluetooth. Evertech also builds custom Autosight devices and companion apps for remote monitoring.

Scherer started Evertech to break complicated problems into core issues and deliver straightforward, affordable solutions designed to last. The firm emphasizes U.S.‑based manufacturing, data security, and a quality‑verified, fast‑shipment model.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic Manufacturing Services (EMS)", "Custom Electronics Engineering", "Electrical Engineering Services", "PCB Manufacturing Services", "PCB Assembly (Surface Mount Technology)", "PCB Assembly (Through Hole)", "Wave Soldering", "Reflow Soldering", "Rapid Prototyping", "3D Printing", "Machining", "Testing & Quality Assurance", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "Low Power Device Design", "Wireless Design (Bluetooth, Wi\u2011Fi, Cellular, GPS, Antennas)", "Embedded Software & Firmware Development", "Extreme Environment Design (High Temperature, Submersion, Steam Sterilization)", "Autosight\u00ae Product Development"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Embedded Electronics", "Wireless IoT Devices", "Industrial Control Boards", "Startups", "OEMs", "Engineering Teams"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SMT Assembly Line (from Electro\u2011Pro acquisition)", "Wave Soldering Equipment", "Reflow Soldering Equipment", "3D Printers", "Machining Equipment", "Full Test Suite"], "volume": "Prototype to full production runs", "lead_time": "< 10 days prototype / 4 weeks production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S. manufacturing in Cedarburg, WI", "Full product design, development, and in\u2011house PCB assembly under one roof", "Prototype turnaround under 10 days; production in 4 weeks", "Autosight\u00ae wireless product line with cellular, Bluetooth, Wi\u2011Fi, and GPS", "Data security and quality\u2011verified shipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2022 by Michael Scherer -> db, /", "Headquarters Cedarburg, WI -> db, /", "Acquired Electro-Pro, Inc. and PCB assembly line -> /", "Autosight product line developed at Tecovan -> /", "Capabilities: SMT, through-hole, wave/reflow, 3D printing, machining -> /", "Lead time: <10 days prototype / 4 weeks production -> /", "Certifications: ISO9001, ROHS -> db", "Industries: medical devices, embedded electronics, wireless IoT, industrial control -> /", "Autosight Asset Tracker for steam autoclave sterilization -> /", "Autosight AC Controller for legacy HVAC integration -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='evertech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FM Corporation was founded in 1980 in Rogers, Arkansas, as a provider of structural foam and injection molded parts. The company remains centrally located in the United States, serving customers nationwide and overseas from its Arkansas headquarters.

The manufacturer operates a 165,000-square-foot main facility that houses both high-pressure and structural foam injection molding, capable of producing parts from 5 ounces to 75 pounds. An in-house finishing department handles sanding, masking, painting, unmasking, and logo application. A 10,000-square-foot climate-controlled assembly area and a separate 40,000-square-foot metals division provide turning, milling, punching, and bending services. Several employees have more than 30 years of tenure with the company.

FM Corporation serves the automotive and aerospace/defense industries, producing components such as automotive parts and manufacturing support trays. The company states it has the ability to serve all industries, though only those two sectors are explicitly named.

