UPDATE companies SET description='Horton, Inc. was founded in 1951 in Britton, South Dakota, when Hugh Schilling acquired the company with backing from three investors. Originally focused on industrial clutches, the business pivoted in the 1960s to apply its clutch expertise to engine cooling for on- and off-highway vehicles.

Today Horton designs and manufactures fan drives, fans, and thermal-management components for heavy-duty applications. The company operates 15 facilities worldwide, serves customers in 70 countries through 900 distributor locations, and produced its 10 millionth fan drive in 2024. Its engineering team uses simulation software and extensive in-house testing to develop customized cooling assemblies that integrate fans, drives, brackets, and hubs.

Horton’s products are used across on-highway and off-highway markets, including commercial trucking, construction, mining, agriculture, stationary power generation, gas compression, and emerging electrification platforms. Major OEMs such as Peterbilt, Kenworth, Freightliner, Navistar, and Volvo have specified Horton fan drives as standard equipment, while fleets and distributors rely on the company’s global sales and service network.

The company attributes its longevity to a collaborative development model that emphasizes listening to customer requirements, then delivering tailored solutions backed by a trained worldwide distributor network. Horton also highlights its environmental focus, noting that its cooling products help reduce fuel consumption and noise while its manufacturing processes aim to eliminate waste and prevent pollution.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','IATF 16949','ISO 27001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engine cooling system design", "Fan drive manufacturing", "Fan manufacturing", "Thermal management engineering", "Custom cooling solution development", "In-house testing and validation", "Application engineering support"], "industries": ["On-Highway", "Off-Highway", "Commercial Trucking", "Construction", "Mining", "Agriculture", "Stationary Power Generation", "Gas Compression", "Electrification"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Collaborative solution development with OEMs", "Extensive in-house testing and simulation capabilities", "Global distributor and dealer network in 70 countries", "Full customization of fan, drive, bracket, and hub assemblies", "Products designed to reduce fuel consumption and noise"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1951 -> db, /about", "Hugh Schilling purchased Horton for $50,000 on September 17, 1951 -> /about", "Originally manufactured industrial clutches -> /about", "Applied clutch expertise to engine cooling in 1960s -> /about", "Fan drives installed to save fuel during 1970s energy crisis -> /about", "Fan drives became standard on Peterbilt, Kenworth, Freightliner, Navistar, Volvo -> /about", "15 facilities worldwide -> /about", "70 countries served -> /about", "900 distributor locations -> /about", "10,000,000th fan drive produced in 2024 -> /about", "Global sales offices in U.S., Canada, Mexico, Germany; representatives in Korea, China, Japan, India, Australia, Columbia, Chile -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 14001, IATF 16949, ISO 27001 -> /about, db", "Industries: trucking, construction, mining, agriculture, generator sectors -> home page", "Industries from form: On-Highway, Off-Highway, Commercial Trucking, Agriculture, Mining, Construction, Stationary/Generators, Electrification -> home page", "Gas compression applications -> home page", "Collaborative solution development emphasis -> /about", "In-house testing resources and simulation tools -> /about", "Global distributor and dealer network -> /about", "Customization of entire cooling solution -> /about", "Environmental responsibility: reduce fuel consumption, noise, waste, pollution -> /about", "Leadership: Cordell Dietz, President and CEO -> /about", "Locations: Roseville, MN; Britton, SD; Schweinfurt, Germany; Oconee, SC; Wuxi, China -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='horton-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='House of Apparel was founded in 1985 in Basehor, Kansas, just outside Kansas City. The company has been family-owned and operated since its inception.

The company provides a full range of custom apparel services including screen printing (up to 10 colors), process printing, screen print transfers, heat sublimation, sublimation transfers, embroidery, patch and emblem production (appliqué, woven, or custom materials), graphic design, logo development, and digitizing. All work is done in-house using automated screen printing presses and multiple embroidery machines. They handle orders from single pieces to large corporate runs, with most orders shipping within seven to ten business days. The shop stocks a wide selection of brand-name apparel from Adidas, Carhartt, Nike, and others.

House of Apparel serves corporate clients, small businesses, and individuals. Their workwear and safety apparel outfit construction crews, restaurant staff, and medical teams, while promotional items support branding for events and trade shows. They also supply hi-visibility safety gear compliant with ANSI/OSHA standards, including vests, shirts, and reflective strips.

The company differentiates itself by keeping all production in-house, using automated presses and multiple embroidery machines to maintain control over quality and turnaround, and by stocking a wide range of brand-name apparel. Customer support follows each order from start to finish to ensure accuracy and on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing (up to 10 colors)", "Process printing", "Screen print transfers", "Heat sublimation", "Sublimation transfers", "Embroidery", "Patch and emblem production (appliqu\u00e9, woven, custom materials)", "Graphic design", "Logo development", "Digitizing", "Custom artwork preparation", "Workwear manufacturing", "Safety apparel (ANSI/OSHA compliant)", "Promotional product decoration"], "industries": ["Corporate", "Construction", "Restaurant/Hospitality", "Medical/Healthcare", "Safety/High-visibility", "Promotional/Events"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated screen printing presses", "Multiple embroidery machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "7-10 business days for most orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All services performed in-house", "Automated screen printing presses and multiple embroidery machines", "Most orders shipped in 7\u201310 business days", "Stocks major brands including Adidas, Carhartt, Nike", "ANSI/OSHA-compliant safety apparel"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1985 -> db, /about", "Located in Basehor, KS -> db, /about", "Family-owned and operated -> homepage", "Services: screen printing, embroidery, patches, heat sublimation, graphic design, digitizing -> /about", "Automated screen printing presses and multiple embroidery machines -> /about", "Turnaround 7-10 business days -> /about", "Brands carried: Adidas, Carhartt, Nike, etc. -> /about", "Industries served: construction, restaurants, medical, corporate, promotional -> /about", "ANSI/OSHA-compliant safety apparel -> /about, db certifications", "Nationwide shipping -> homepage"], "company_typ