UPDATE companies SET description='Hub Manufacturing operates from a 30,000-square-foot facility in Minneapolis, Minnesota, where it has produced precision metal stampings and fabrications since 1956. The company remains family-owned after three generations, with Brad Hendrickson running the shop floor day-to-day and walking the production lines himself.

The shop runs a full range of metal forming processes under one ISO 9001:2015-certified roof: progressive, compound, and hand-transfer stamping on presses from 6 to 800 tons; hydraulic draw and deep-draw forming up to 0.500-inch thickness; flat-sheet and tube laser cutting; CNC tube bending; press brake forming; in-house tool and die design, build, and maintenance; a dedicated welding cell for mild steel, stainless, and aluminum assemblies; and final packaging and fulfillment. The operation handles prototype through high-volume runs, with bed sizes from 12×12 to 96×72 inches.

Hub serves OEMs in defense and military (ruggedized housings, armor-grade brackets), aerospace and marine, automotive, agriculture (structural stampings for implements), construction and machinery, and Tier 1 and Tier 2 supply chains. Customers include defense contractors and agricultural equipment manufacturers who require traceability, consistency, and domestic sourcing.

The company emphasizes its “Can Do” model — no subcontracting, in-house tooling from napkin sketch to production die, and a one-business-day quote turnaround — to keep lead times short and quality tight. Being 100 percent U.S.-owned and operated is presented as a deliberate choice to avoid offshore delays and finger-pointing between vendors.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal stamping", "Hydraulic draw forming", "Deep draw stamping", "Progressive stamping", "Compound stamping", "Hand-transfer stamping", "Sheet laser cutting", "Tube laser cutting", "CNC tube bending", "Press brake forming", "In-house tool & die build and maintenance", "Welding (assemblies)", "Assembly", "Packaging & fulfillment", "Custom packaging", "Short run production", "Long run production", "Prototyping", "First article inspection", "ISO 9001:2015 quality inspection"], "industries": ["Defense & Military", "Aerospace & Marine", "Automotive", "Agriculture", "Construction & Machinery", "Tier 1 suppliers", "Tier 2 suppliers", "OEMs"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper", "Nylon", "Mild steel"], "equipment": ["Tube laser cutting machine", "CNC tube bender", "Press brake", "Hydraulic forming presses", "Heavy-tonnage stamping presses (6-800 tons)", "Progressive die sets", "Compound die sets", "Hand-transfer die sets", "Welding cell"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool & die build and maintenance", "All metal fabrication processes under one roof (stamping, laser cutting, CNC bending, welding, assembly)", "Family-owned and operated since 1956", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "Quote turnaround within one business day"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1956 -> db", "Headquarters Minneapolis, Minnesota -> db", "Family-owned, three generations -> /", "Brad Hendrickson runs shop floor -> /", "30,000+ sq ft facility -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Press capacity 6-800 tons -> /", "Thickness up to 0.500 inch -> /", "In-house tool & die build and maintenance -> /", "Tube laser, CNC tube bender, press brake, welding cell -> /", "Industries: Defense, Aerospace, Marine, Automotive, Agriculture, Construction, Machinery -> /", "Materials: carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, copper, nylon -> /", "Quote within 1 business day -> /", "All processes under one roof, no subcontracting -> /", "100% U.S.-owned and operated -> /", "Prototype through high-volume -> /", "Bed sizes 12x12 to 96x72 inches -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hub-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Illini Wire Works, Inc. operates from Olney, Illinois, where it was founded in 1998 as a family‑owned and veteran‑owned business.

The shop produces custom wire forms, industrial fan guards, and agriculture wire products. Its capabilities span more than a dozen wire‑shaping processes, including bending, flattening, heading, piercing, extruding, swaging, upsetting, drilling, threading, welding, roll forming, and chamfering, supported by a 3D Aim Machine. The facility handles orders from simple bolts to complex assemblies requiring multiple operations.

Primary markets include industrial equipment manufacturers needing fan guards, agricultural operations requiring durable wire products, and commercial clients seeking custom wire fabrication. The company also serves customers within a 100‑mile radius with curbside pickup and delivery.

Illini Wire Works emphasizes its combined experience and “practically limitless” wire‑creation capabilities, positioning itself as a full‑service partner that manages every step from order placement to delivery. All products are made in the USA.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bending", "Flattening", "Heading", "Piercing", "Extruding", "Swaging", "Upsetting", "Drilling", "Threading", "Welding", "Roll forming", "Chamfering", "3D Aim Machine"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Agriculture", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3D Aim Machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Curbside pickup and delivery within 100 miles", "Family and veteran owned", "Products made in the USA", "Over a dozen wire\u2011shaping techniques", "Full\u2011service wire fabrication shop"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Olney, Illinois -> db, /about", "Family and veteran owned -> db, /, /about", "Custom wire forms, industrial fan guards, agriculture wire products -> /", "Wire shaping processes (bending, flattening, heading, piercing, extruding, swaging, upsetting, drilling, threading, welding, roll forming, chamfering) -> /capabilities", "3D Aim Machine -> /capabilities", "Curbside pickup and delivery within 100 miles -> /", "Products made in the USA -> /", "Member of Richland County Chamber of Commerce -> /about", "Member of Wire Fabricators Association -> /about", "Serves industrial, agricultural, commercial customers -> /, /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='illini-wire-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Imagineering, Inc. was founded in 1986 in Elk Grove Village, Illinois.

The company specializes in PCB fabrication and assembly, offering services from rapid prototyping to high-volume production. Its capabilities include rigid, flex, and rigid-flex board fabrication up to 50 layers, high-density interconnect (HDI) technology, and a range of surface-mount, through-hole, and advanced package assembly processes. Imagineering operates production facilities at its Illinois headquarters and uses offshore partners in Korea and Taiwan for scalable output. The company reports serving 30,000 customers, shipping 20 million unique part numbers, and producing 150 million individual pieces annually, with over 9,000 prototype designs transitioned to production in the most recent year.

Imagineering serves customers across medical, defense, consumer electronics, and aerospace industries, among others. Its client base ranges from hobbyist builders to international electronics manufacturers, including OEMs with regulated compliance requirements such as ITAR and AS9100D.

The company emphasizes a single-point-of-contact model that integrates fabrication, assembly, component procurement, and testing. It promotes same-day prototype turnaround, a 100% on-time delivery guarantee, and compliance with aerospace and defense standards as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ITAR Registered','RoHS Compliant','IPC Member','UL Approved','WEEE Certified','CCR Registered','ORCA Registered','SAM Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB fabrication (rigid, flex, rigid-flex)", "High-density interconnect (HDI) fabrication", "PCB assembly (surface mount technology)", "PCB assembly (through-hole technology)", "BGA and micro-BGA assembly", "Flip chip assembly", "Flex circuit assembly", "Cable and wire harness assembly", "Turnkey assembly (component procurement, fabrication, assembly, test)", "Consignment assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) analysis", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "RF testing", "Functional testing", "Rapid prototyping (same-day)", "High-volume production", "Impedance control", "Stacked microvias"], "industries": ["Medical", "Defense", "Consumer electronics", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["FR-4 Standard", "Multifunctional 130 Tg", "FR-4 High 170 Tg", "Getek 170Tg", "NAN-YA NPG-R/NPG-TL", "ISOLA410", "Rogers 4000", "Thermal Clad (including Aluminum Bonding)", "Nelco4000-13160Tg", "Allied 408 180 Tg", "Polyimide230Tg", "BT Epoxy 180Tg", "Teflon", "Taconic", "Arion", "Flex materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production; 9,000+ prototype designs transitioned to production annually", "lead_time": "Same-day prototypes; small production runs in 5-7 days; medium-to-large production in 2-3 weeks", "tolerances": "Hole tolerances: standard \u00b10.004 in, press fit \u00b10.002 in; trace/space minimums from 0.003 in (0.5 oz copper) to 0.012 in (4 oz copper)", "built_on": ["Same-day prototype turnaround", "100% on-time delivery guarantee",