UPDATE companies SET description='Indigo Metal Fabrication began in 2015 in a garage in Portland, Oregon, founded by Willy and Amber. The husband-and-wife team moved the operation to Troutdale, Oregon, where they continue to run the shop with a focus on integrity and community. Willy brings over twelve years of professional welding experience and holds ASME certification in MIG and TIG processes, while Amber oversees aesthetics and procedures.

The shop specializes in one-off custom metal fabrication using salvaged materials sourced from the Pacific Northwest. Core capabilities include CNC plasma cutting, MIG and TIG welding, and design services. They are particularly known for adventure vehicle modifications, building durable, inspired pieces for overlanding and off-road enthusiasts. The operation remains small-scale, having grown from a garage to a dedicated shop space.

They consider projects of any size, from small brackets to full vehicle overhauls.

