UPDATE companies SET description='Journey Electronics Corp. was founded in 1983 in Monroe, Ohio, as a family-owned operation focused on printed circuit board fabrication and assembly. The company began as a small shop and has grown into a recognized Midwest electronics manufacturer.

The company provides surface mount (SMT) and through-hole PCB assembly, PCB fabrication through partners, first article and functional testing, automated optical inspection, wire harness and cable assembly, box build, and PCB design and layout services. It handles low- to mid-volume runs of 50 to 1,000-plus pieces, along with prototype and new product introduction builds, and offers redesign, modification, and rework for existing assemblies.

Journey Electronics serves industrial automation and control, test and measurement, consumer electronics, lighting and LED systems, automotive, industrial equipment, construction equipment, textile labeling, high-speed inkjet press manufacturing, and other OEMs. Past customers cited include NCR, Corning, 3M, NASA, and Kodak, and the company has built controls for welding systems, spectroscopy, moisture control, additive feeders, dimensional inspection, banking and ATM systems, conveyor management, heat transfer, touch sensing, and high-powered LED lighting.

The company emphasizes its IPC-A-610 and IPC-A-600 trained assembly processes, ANSI/ESD S20.20-2021 compliant facility, and RoHS-compliant manufacturing since 2006. As a family-owned business, it highlights personalized service, flexible turnkey or consignment manufacturing, competitive pricing, and consistent on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI/ESD S20.20-2021','IPC-A-610','IPC-A-600','RoHS compliant','UL-94V-0']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface mount technology (SMT) assembly", "Through-hole assembly", "PCB fabrication (via partners)", "First article inspection", "Functional testing", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "Visual inspection", "Wire harness manufacturing", "Custom cable assemblies", "Box build / complete unit assembly", "PCB design and layout", "CAD drawing creation and editing", "Product development and design", "Rework, modification, and redesign of existing PCB assemblies", "Component sourcing", "Consignment builds", "Automated wire cutting and stripping", "Automated lead cutting and forming", "Reflow soldering", "Wave soldering", "Hand soldering", "0402 component placement", "Lead-free (Pb-free) assembly", "UL-94V-0 flame retardant PCBs"], "industries": ["Industrial automation and control", "Test and measurement", "Consumer electronics", "Lighting and LED systems", "Automotive", "Industrial equipment manufacturing", "Construction equipment manufacturing", "Textile labeling, transfers and emblems", "High-speed inkjet press manufacturing", "OEM (original equipment manufacturer)", "High-current applications", "Electronic manufacturing", "Banking and ATM control systems", "Conveyor management", "Controlled heat transfer systems", "Touch sensing controls", "High-powered LED lighting", "Welding system controls", "Spectroscopy", "Moisture control", "Additive systems and feeder controllers", "Dimensional measurement and inspection systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["High-speed SMT placement equipment", "Wave soldering mach