UPDATE companies SET description='Kaiser Manufacturing Inc. was founded in 1960 in West St. Paul, Minnesota, as a family-owned and operated industrial textile manufacturer. The company has remained under family ownership since its inception, focusing on custom textile products for industrial clients.

The company operates a facility equipped with more than 80 cutting and sewing machines and employs over 40 people. Its core services include industrial sewing, die cutting, programmable cutting, and heat sealing using both ultrasound and hot air welders. Kaiser Manufacturing produces a range of custom textile components such as straps, protective pads, bags, covers, filters, air diffusers, fabric ducting, and multi-material assemblies, along with specialty packaging.

Kaiser Manufacturing serves industrial customers requiring custom sewn, cut, and sealed textile products. Its product offerings address needs in applications such as protective padding, filtration, air handling, and multi-material assemblies, though specific industry sectors are not publicly detailed.

The company emphasizes its ISO 9001:2015 certification and a commitment to quality, collaboration, and customer service as the foundation of its six-decade track record.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial sewing", "Die cutting", "Programmable cutting", "Ultrasound heat sealing", "Hot air heat sealing", "Specialty packaging"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Specialty fabrics", "Industrial textiles"], "equipment": ["Industrial sewing machines", "Die cutting machines", "Programmable cutting machine (computerized)", "Ultrasound welder", "Hot air welder"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Family-owned continuity since 1960", "In-house die cutting, programmable cutting, and heat sealing (ultrasound and hot air)", "Over 80 cutting and sewing machines for production capacity"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1960 -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Headquarters in West St. Paul, Minnesota -> db", "40+ employees -> db", "80+ cutting and sewing machines -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> db", "Services: industrial sewing, die cutting, programmable cutting, heat sealing (ultrasound and hot air) -> /", "Products: straps, protective pads, bags, covers, filters, air diffusers, fabric ducting, multi-material assemblies, specialty fabrics -> /", "Commitment to quality, collaboration, customer service -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kaiser-manufacturing-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kapstone Medical, LLC was founded in 2007 by John Kapitan in Charlotte, North Carolina. After 15 years as a design engineer and regulatory affairs executive in the medical device industry—including a founding role at spinal implant company Altiva Corporation—Kapitan established the firm to provide a single-source solution for medical device commercialization. The company remains founder-led, with Kapitan serving as CEO alongside a management team that includes COO Mike Burgan, Director of Business Development Hayden Kapitan, and Director of Engineering David Considine.

The company operates as a full-service partner covering the entire product lifecycle: Phase 0 feasibility, design and engineering, prototyping, testing, intellectual property, human factors engineering, quality system implementation, regulatory strategy and submission, and commercialization support. Through its subsidiary Kapstone Manufacturing, it added ISO 13485 contract manufacturing and in-house additive manufacturing with DLyte dry electropolishing, eliminating the need to outsource prototype fabrication. The Charlotte facility has supported over 200 customers, 150 product launches, and more than 100 regulatory submissions across U.S. and EU markets.

Kapstone serves medical device startups, physician entrepreneurs, R&D firms, and established OEMs, with a focus on orthopedics, spinal implants, and surgical instruments. Notable engagements include a Phase 0 feasibility study for SealJect Medical, design and manufacturing of prone lateral spinal access instruments and spinal fusion implants for a medical device firm, and quality system development for an R&D company preparing for contract manufacturing.

The firm’s differentiation stems from its integrated “one-stop” model, which Kapitan created after recognizing that outsourced prototyping was the primary friction point for clients. By bringing manufacturing in-house under the same quality system, Kapstone aims to reduce hand-offs, accelerate turnaround, and maintain regulatory continuity from prototype through commercial distribution.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','CE Mark']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Phase 0 Feasibility Studies", "Medical Device Design & Engineering", "Prototyping & Testing", "Intellectual Property Strategy", "Human Factors Engineering & Usability", "Formative & Summative Evaluation", "User Research & Context of Use Analysis", "UI/UX & Industrial Design for MedTech", "Quality Management System Development & Implementation", "eQMS Implementation", "Quality Gap Analysis & Auditing", "Regulatory Strategy & Submission (FDA/EU)", "Regulatory Compliance Remediation", "Regulatory Training", "Additive Manufacturing & Finishing", "DLyte Dry Electropolishing", "Supply Chain Management", "Design for Manufacturing", "Commercialization Strategy & Market Entry", "Product Launch Support", "Ongoing Operations Support"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Orthopedics", "Spinal Implants", "Surgical Instruments", "MedTech", "Research & Development"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["DLyte Dry Electropolishing System"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source solution spanning design, regulatory, quality, manufacturing, and commercialization", "In-house ISO 13485 contract manufacturing via Kapstone Manufacturing subsidiary", "Integrated DLyte dry electropolishing for additive manufactured parts", "End-to-end services from Phase 0 feasibility through commercial launch", "US and EU regulatory expertise with 100+ submissions"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 by John Kapitan -> /about-us", "Headquarters Charlotte, North Carolina -> /about-us, db", "ISO 13485 and CE Mark certifications -> db certifications", "Full-service capabilities: NPD, QA, RA, Manufacturing, Commercialization -> /", "Subsidiary Kapstone Manufacturing provides ISO 13485 contract manufacturing -> /", "In-house DLyte dry electropolishing for additive manufacturing -> /", "200+ customers served, 150+ products launched, 100+ regulatory submissions -> /", "Management team: John Kapitan (CEO), Mike Burgan (COO), Hayden Kapitan (Dir. Bus Dev), David Considine (Dir. Engineering) -> /about-us", "Serves medical device startups, surgeons, OEMs; examples: SealJect Medical, spinal instrument firm, R&D company -> /", "Focus on orthopedics, spinal implants, surgical instruments -> /about-us, /", "Mission: single-source solution to eliminate outsourcing friction -> /", "John Kapitan prior founding member of Altiva Corporation -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kapstone-medical-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Keco Inc was founded in 1963 by the Keister brothers as an injection molding shop in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. Chris White joined the company as an engineer in 1994, became general manager in 2000, and purchased the business in 2004; he remains owner and president. The company operates as a single, engineering-led facility where molding, assembly, engineering, and fulfillment share the same shop floor.

The company provides full-service contract manufacturing centered on plastic injection molding across a 28- to 1,100-ton press range, supporting prototype, short-run, and high-volume production. In-house capabilities extend to tooling sourcing and validation, product engineering review and manufacturability analysis, mechanical and low-voltage electro-mechanical assembly, functional testing, packaging, kitting, inventory management, and direct-to-customer fulfillment. Over the past decade Keco has shipped more than 100,000 orders from its Oklahoma City plant.

Keco serves OEMs in industrial equipment, oil and gas, automotive aftermarket, foodservice equipment, architectural and electrical products, and consumer goods. Documented programs include collision repair products (SEMA Award 2022), oilfield spill containment systems in continuous production since 1992, architectural lighting assemblies since 1973, consumer plumbing tools fulfilled through Amazon FBA, and plant saucers for direct-to-consumer and wholesale channels.

Keco differentiates itself through an engineering-led operating model where decisions are made by staff who understand the product, tooling, and process. It offers a single accountable team from prototype through customer delivery, a broad tonnage range on one floor, and U.S.-based production in Oklahoma City. The company emphasizes total program cost over piece price, combining domestic molding with assembly, inventory, and fulfillment to reduce risk and ensure repeatability, fast problem solving, and dependable supply.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding (prototype, short-run, high-volume)", "Insert molding and over-molding", "Tooling sourcing, build oversight, validation, maintenance, repair, and transfer", "Product engineering review and manufacturability analysis", "Material selection guidance", "Mechanical assembly", "Low-voltage electro-mechanical assembly", "Plastic and metal integration", "Functional testing", "Finishing and pack-out", "Kitting and packaging", "Inventory management", "Direct-to-customer fulfillment", "Warehousing and shipping", "Reshoring support (tool evaluation, transfer, qualification, production ramp)"], "industries": ["Industrial Equipment", "Oil & Gas", "Automotive Aftermarket", "Foodservice & Equipment", "Architectural & Electrical", "Consumer Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["28\u20131,100 ton injection molding presses"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering-led operation with technical accountability close to the customer", "One accountable team from prototype to customer doorstep", "Broad press tonnage range (28\u20131,100 tons) on a single shop floor", "U.S.-based production integrating molding, assembly, inventory, and fulfillment", "Focus on total program cost reduction through consolidated domestic operations"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 by Keister brothers -> /about", "Chris White joined 1994, GM 2000, purchased 2004 -> /about", "Single Oklahoma City facility with engineering, molding, assembly, fulfillment -> /, /about", "Press tonnage range 28\u20131,100 tons -> /, /about", "100,000+ orders shipped in past 10 years -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> /, db", "Industries served: Industrial Equipment, Oil & Gas, Automotive Aftermarket, Foodservice & Equipment, Architectural & Electrical, Consumer Products -> /", "Case studies: KECO Body Repair Products (SEMA 2022), Pollution Control Corp (since 1992), Roberts Step-Lite (since 1973), Flange Off (Amazon FBA), Rhino Saucers (e-commerce/wholesale) -> /", "Capabilities: injection molding, tooling, engineering support, assembly, logistics, fulfillment, reshoring -> /", "Differentiators: engineering-led, one accountable team, broad tonnage, U.S.-based, prototype-to-customer, long-term thinking -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keco-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Keystone Electronics Inc. was founded in 1989 in York, Pennsylvania. No founders or ownership structure are disclosed in public materials.

The firm specializes in custom electronic assembly, offering electro-mechanical assembly, cable and harness fabrication, printed circuit board assembly, and general contract manufacturing. Its service lineup also includes quality control and ISO 9001 certified processes. Facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not publicly disclosed.

Keystone serves a wide range of industries that require electronic assembly, though specific sectors or named customers are not listed in its public materials. The company emphasizes its ability to support diverse manufacturing needs through its assembly and integration capabilities.

The company’s stated differentiation rests on a philosophy that quality must be built in rather than inspected in, coupled with a focus on delivering cost-effective solutions. Its long track record — over 20 years of experience as of 2019 — and ISO 9001 certification are presented as evidence of consistent quality standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electro-mechanical assembly", "Cable and harness assembly", "Printed circuit board assembly", "Contract manufacturing", "Quality control"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quality built into the manufacturing process, not just inspected afterward", "ISO 9001 certified quality management system", "Cost-effective custom electronic assembly", "Integrated electro-mechanical, cable/harness, and PCB assembly services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 -> db", "Headquarters York, Pennsylvania -> db", "Certification ISO 9001 -> db", "Services: electro-mechanical, cable and harness, PC board assembly, contract work -> homepage (path ''/'')", "Description: quality built in, cost-effective, since 1989 -> db description", "Custom electronic assembly -> homepage title (path ''/'')", "Over 20 years experience as of 2019 -> homepage text (path ''/'')", "Commitment to detail and quality standards -> homepage text (path ''/'')"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keystone-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kimball Electronics Inc. was founded in 1921 in Salt Lake City, Utah, as a wholesale distributor of electronic components. The company has operated continuously for over a century, establishing a presence in the electromechanical field and expanding to multiple locations across the Intermountain West.

The firm distributes a broad range of electronic parts and provides value-added services including supply chain solutions, quality assurance testing, and global sourcing. It operates branches in Salt Lake City, Utah; Boise, Idaho; and Lakewood, Colorado, serving customers across those regions. The Salt Lake City branch holds ISO 9001:2015 certification, and the company emphasizes rigorous component testing to ensure reliability.

Kimball Electronics serves customers in the electromechanical and high-end appliance sectors, supplying components for electronic manufacturing and appliance production. Its linecard includes products from a variety of electronic component manufacturers, and the company highlights its ability to source hard-to-find parts.

The company states its mission is to be flexible, responsive, and dedicated as the company of choice for customers, employees, and suppliers through innovative products and process solutions. This mission, along with a stated commitment to excellence and innovation, is presented as the foundation of its long-term customer relationships.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Supply chain solutions", "Quality assurance testing", "Global sourcing", "Appliance parts supply"], "industries": ["Electromechanical components", "High-end appliances", "Electronics manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certification at Salt Lake City branch", "Over 100 years of wholesale distribution experience", "Multi-location network across Utah, Idaho, and Colorado", "Global sourcing access to diverse supplier network", "Rigorous component testing and quality assurance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1921 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Salt Lake City, Utah -> db, /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> db, /about", "Multiple locations: Salt Lake City, Boise, Lakewood -> /about", "Services: Supply Chain Solutions, Quality Assurance, Global Sourcing -> /about", "Mission statement -> /about", "Industries: electromechanical, high-end appliances -> /about, /", "Over 100 years experience -> description, /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kimball-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kinney Industries Inc has operated from Huntsville, Alabama since its founding in 1972. The company is an ISO 9001:2015 and ITAR registered small business serving the contract electronics manufacturing market.

The firm provides a range of manufacturing services including cable and wire harness assemblies (signal, power, and RF cables from prototype to high volume), electromechanical assemblies such as power distribution units, radios, diagnostic equipment, power supplies, and drone tethers, as well as CNC machining (vertical milling, lathe, and plunge/sinker EDM), injection molding using vertical equipment with in-house mold design and machining, over-molding and encapsulation, and engineering services spanning electrical, electronic, mechanical, industrial, and software development. Testing capabilities cover continuity, hi-pot, RF, and customized test programs, supported by the company''s proprietary HT-128+ wireless harness tester.

The company differentiates itself through turnkey injection molding solutions, in-house tooling development, and the HT-128+ tester designed to reduce downstream test failures for installed wiring harnesses. It emphasizes short cycle times from concept to production and offers prototyping through full-rate production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract Manufacturing", "Engineering Services (Electrical, Electronic, Mechanical, Industrial, Software)", "CNC Vertical Milling", "CNC Lathe", "Plunge/Sinker Electrical Discharge Machining (EDM)", "Injection Molding (Vertical)", "Over-molding", "Backshell Overmolding/Encapsulation", "Mold Design and Machining", "Cable and Wire Harness Assembly", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Continuity Testing", "Hi-Pot Testing", "RF Testing", "Customized Testing", "Prototyping", "Documentation Services", "Production Testing", "Component Encapsulation", "Laser Part Marking", "Electrical and Wiring Integration"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Electronics", "Unmanned Aerial Systems", "Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC Vertical Milling Centers", "Horizontal 2-Axis CNC Lathe", "Vertical Injection Molding Equipment", "HT-128+ Handheld Wiring Analyzer"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 -> db", "Headquarters Huntsville, Alabama -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 registered -> website: /", "ITAR registered -> website: /", "Small Business -> website: /", "Cable and wire harness assemblies prototype to high volume -> website: /", "Electromechanical assemblies: power distribution units, radios, diagnostic equipment, power supplies, drone tethers -> website: /", "CNC machining: vertical milling, lathe, EDM -> website: /", "Injection molding turnkey with vertical equipment -> website: /", "Engineering services: electrical, electronic, mechanical, industrial, software -> website: /", "Testing: continuity, hi-pot, RF, customized -> website: /", "HT-128+ wireless harness tester developed for installed wiring harnesses -> website: /", "Aerospace case study for HT-128+ -> website: /", "In-house mold design and machining -> website: /", "Equipment: CNC Vertical Milling Centers, Horizontal 2-Axis CNC Lathe, Vertical Injection Molding Equipment, HT-128+ Handheld Wiring Analyzer -> website: /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kinney-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The operation began in 1984 as American Fabricators, Inc., and today functions as the only Kloeckner Metals site dedicated exclusively to value-added fabrication rather than raw material distribution. It is owned by Kloeckner Metals Corporation, a subsidiary of the German-based Klöckner & Co SE Group.

The plant employs over 150 associates and houses 17 Amada turret punches, four Amada lasers (including 6 kW and 4 kW fiber and two 4 kW CO₂ units), 24 Amada press brakes up to 220 metric tons, a 60-ton robotic press brake, a Panasonic TM-2000WG III robotic welding arm, and a Prima Power BCe Smart Panel Bender. Capabilities span laser cutting, forming, MIG/TIG/resistance spot welding, hardware insertion, mechanical assembly, and metal finishing such as media blasting, tumbling, grinding, graining, and polishing. Materials processed include hot-rolled pickled and oiled, cold rolled, galvanized, galvannealed, aluminized, prepainted, electro-galvanized, aluminum, and stainless steels.

The facility serves the food-service, transportation, HVAC, hot-water-heater, and appliance industries. Examples from the branch include stainless-steel fan mounts for food service, galvanized mounting brackets and door-frame headers for transportation, stainless drain pans and pre-painted galvanized posts for HVAC, hot-rolled plate disc plates for water heaters, and cosmetic stainless parts for appliances.

The company emphasizes its in-house welder qualification program based on AWS D1.1, advanced inspection tools, and a workforce where over half the associates have tenured more than ten years. Special programs include Kanban, stocking, quick-turn prototypes, and PPAP support, all backed by the global supply-chain strength of Kloeckner Metals.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Forming", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Resistance spot welding", "Hardware insertion", "Mechanical assembly", "Media blasting", "Abrasive tumbling", "Grinding", "Metal graining", "Polishing", "Turret punching", "Press braking", "Robotic welding", "Panel bending", "Quick-turn prototypes", "PPAP", "Kanban", "Stocking programs"], "industries": ["Food service", "Transportation", "HVAC", "Hot water heater", "Appliance"], "materials": ["HRP&O (Hot Rolled Pickled and Oiled)", "Cold Rolled Steel", "Galvanized Steel", "Galvannealed Steel", "Aluminized Steel", "Prepainted Steel", "Electro-Galvanized Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel", "Coated Steel", "Plastic Sheet"], "equipment": ["17 Amada Turret Punches", "4 Amada Lasers (6 kW Fiber, 4 kW Fiber, 2\u00d74 kW CO\u2082)", "24 Amada Press Brakes (up to 220 metric tons)", "1 Robotic Press Brake (60-ton)", "Panasonic TM-2000WG III Robotic Welding Arm", "Prima Power BCe Smart Panel Bender"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only Kloeckner site dedicated exclusively to value-added fabrication", "In-house welder qualification program per AWS D1.1", "Kanban, stocking, quick-turn prototype, and PPAP programs", "115,000 sq ft facility with 17 Amada turret punches, 4 Amada lasers, 24 press brakes", "Strategic location near major interstates serving 50% of U.S. population"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1984 -> db", "Headquarters in Lebanon, Tennessee -> db", "115,000 sq ft facility -> /", "Over 150 skilled associates -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Only Kloeckner site dedicated exclusively to value-added fabrication -> /", "17 Amada Turret Punches -> /", "4 Amada Lasers (6 kW Fiber, 4 kW Fiber, 2\u00d74 kW CO\u2082) -> /", "24 Amada Press Brakes up to 220 metric tons -> /", "1 Robotic Press Brake (60-ton) -> /", "Panasonic TM-2000WG III Robotic Welding Arm -> /", "Prima Power BCe Smart Panel Bender -> /", "Welding: MIG, TIG, Resistance Spot -> /", "Hardware insertion (threaded standoffs, self-locking nuts, blind standoffs, Penn Engineering) -> /", "Assembly (mechanical fastening, hinge installation, locking mechanisms, latches) -> /", "Metal finishing (media blasting, abrasive tumblers, grinding, metal graining, polishing) -> /", "Materials: HRP&O, cold rolled, galvanized, galvannealed, aluminized, prepaint, electro-galvanized, aluminum, stainless -> /", "Industries: food service (fan mount), transportation (mounting bracket, door frame header), HVAC (drain pan, post, header plate, bracket), hot water heater (disc plate), appliance (cosmetic stainless parts) -> /", "Special programs: Kanban, Stocking program, Quick turn/prototypes, PPAPs -> /", "In-house welder qualification based on AWS D1.1 -> /", "Over half associates with 10+ years tenure -> /", "Strategic location 30 minutes from Nashville with access to major distribution corridors -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kloeckner-metals-nashville-american-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Koller Craft Plastic Products, a division of Koller Enterprises, has operated from Fenton, Missouri since 1941 when A.J. Koller Sr. founded the company as a custom molder. The family-owned business, now in its third generation, adopted the "Craft" name to reflect the pride and craftsmanship its founder valued. The company maintains a second facility in Gadsden, Alabama.

Its capabilities include gas-assist molding, over-molding, manual and automated assembly, and decorating services such as hot stamping. The company also offers engineering support with design optimization and rapid prototyping, material sourcing, and tooling maintenance.

Koller Craft serves the automotive, agriculture and lawn & garden, general industrial, and material handling sectors.

The company emphasizes its ISO 9001 certification, held since April 2003, and a total quality system guided by 80/20 principles. Domestic production is cited as a differentiator, enabling quicker delivery and rapid problem resolution, while a focus on on-time shipping and quick problem resolution rounds out its value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Gas Assist Injection Molding", "Over Molding", "Assembly (manual and automated)", "Hot Stamp Decorating", "Engineering Design Optimization", "Rapid Prototyping", "Material Sourcing", "Tooling & Maintenance"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Agriculture/Lawn & Garden", "General Industrial", "Material Handling"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics", "Thermosets"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (80\u20132,200 tons)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001 certified since April 2003", "Family-owned, third-generation operation since 1941", "Full-service offering: engineering, material sourcing, tooling & maintenance", "Domestic production for faster delivery and rapid problem-solving"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1941 by A.J. Koller Sr. -> /about", "Family-owned, third-generation -> /about", "Headquarters Fenton, MO -> db", "Midwest facility: 132,000 sq ft, 22 presses (88-2200 tons), 85 employees -> /about", "South facility: 213,000 sq ft, 31 presses (80-1500 tons), 120 employees -> /about", "ISO 9001 certified April 2003 -> /", "Capabilities: Injection Molding, Assembly, Decorating -> /capabilities", "Services: Engineering, Material Sourcing, Tooling & Maintenance -> /services", "Gas Assist Injection Molding -> /", "Over molding -> /products", "Hot Stamp decorating -> /products", "Industries: Automotive, Agriculture/Lawn & Garden, General Industrial, Material Handling -> /", "Top customer Watlow -> /", "Made in USA commitment -> /about", "80/20 principles -> /about", "Koller Enterprises five manufacturing operations -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='koller-craft-plastic-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Landmark Manufacturing Corporation operates from Gallatin, Missouri, where it was founded in 1953 by the Critten family as Longwood Furnace. The business began as a furnace company before expanding into nationwide distribution in 1974 and entering the metal fabrication subcontracting market in 1978.

Today Landmark provides custom metal fabrication with start-to-finish capabilities that include stamping (presses up to 2,000 tons), robotic welding, laser cutting, horizontal machining, CNC press braking, electrostatic E-Coat painting, and assembly. The facility spans more than 650,000 square feet and houses stamping, forming, bending, welding, tooling, engineering, quality control, warehousing, and shipping departments. The company reports having fabricated thousands of different components for hundreds of customers over its history.

Its customer base includes manufacturers of agricultural and construction equipment (Kubota), outdoor power equipment (Excel Industries), and commercial trailers (Meritor), as evidenced by supplier awards from those companies. Landmark serves a range of industrial sectors requiring heavy-gauge metal stampings, welded assemblies, and finished components.

Its stated mission focuses on on-time delivery, continuous improvement, and long-term partnerships with customers and suppliers.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Stamping (up to 2,000 ton)", "Forming", "Bending", "Robotic Welding", "Laser Cutting (fiber laser up to 10,000 watt)", "Horizontal Machining", "CNC Press Brake (120 ton)", "Electrostatic Paint (E-Coat)", "Assembly", "Tooling & Engineering", "Quality Assurance (ISO 9001:2015)", "Warehousing & Shipping", "Laser Oxide Removal", "3D Scanning (precision measurement)"], "industries": ["Agricultural equipment", "Construction equipment", "Outdoor power equipment", "Commercial trailer manufacturing", "Industrial machinery"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["2,000 ton stamping press", "1,500 ton stamping press", "1,000 ton stamping press", "600 ton stamping press", "120 ton CNC press brake", "Panasonic PerformArc Robotic Welding System", "Articulating Manipulating Arm", "Trumpf 2,600 watt laser", "Mitsubishi LVP 4,000 watt laser", "Mitsubishi 3015GX-F 10,000 watt Fiber Laser", "Mitsubishi Vertical Milling Machines", "FARO Edge 7-axis Precision Measuring Equipment", "Scantech KSCAN 3-D Scanners", "Uni Roller / Servo Roll Feeder and Conveyor", "Servo feeder with Attachments", "Laser Oxide Removal Machine", "Electrostatic Paint System (E-Coat line)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Start-to-finish metal fabrication: stamping, welding, laser cutting, machining, E-Coat finishing", "Stamping capacity up to 2,000 tons", "Robotic welding cells with Panasonic PerformArc systems", "Over 650,000 sq ft facility with in-house tooling and engineering"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1953 by Critten family as Longwood Furnace -> /about-us", "Renamed Landmark Manufacturing Corporation in 1986 -> /about-us", "Facility over 650,000 sq ft -> /", "Stamping presses up to 2,000 ton -> /", "Robotic welding, laser cutting, horizontal machining centers -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /quality", "Awards from Kubota, Excel Industries, Meritor -> /", "Equipment list: Trumpf laser, Mitsubishi lasers, FARO Edge, Scantech scanners, etc. -> /about-us", "Mission and quality policy -> /quality", "Headquarters Gallatin, Missouri -> db", "Founded year 1953 -> db", "Certifications ISO9001 -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='landmark-manufacturing-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Linear Manufacturing has operated from Colorado Springs, Colorado since its founding in 1995.

The company provides full-service electronics contract manufacturing, spanning surface-mount technology (SMT) assembly, through-hole assembly, mixed-technology PCB assembly, box build, and rapid prototyping. Its SMT lines handle components down to 0.0402 package size, with plans to reach 0.0201, and support both low- and high-volume throughput, single- and double-sided placement, BGA placement and rework, and fine-pitch placement. Engineering design services are delivered through a long-standing partnership with KS Technologies, a Colorado Springs firm specializing in mobile hardware accessories, applications, and cloud services; both companies hold Apple MFi certification. Linear also offers design-for-manufacturing (DFM), design-for-test (DFT), and design-for-assembly (DFA) support, turnkey and consigned material management, statistical process control, and comprehensive inspection and test. The facility employs IPC-610 certified operators, though total headcount is not published.

Linear serves original equipment manufacturers across aerospace, oil and gas, medical devices, Bluetooth and GPS technology, water and wastewater treatment, security devices, controllers, sensors, cleaning equipment, and irrigation controllers. Case studies illustrate work for an oil and gas company needing pipeline-monitoring electronics, an asset-tracking startup that met a Consumer Electronics Show deadline, a medical device firm achieving FDA compliance on legacy boards, an aerospace customer requiring legacy product duplication with counterfeit-part prevention, and a wastewater treatment company completing an abandoned design.

The company states its differentiation lies in turnkey solutions that free customers to focus on innovation, strategic supplier alliances that improve pricing and accountability, a commitment to U.S.-based manufacturing at high quality standards, and a culture described as "real people doing business with real people."', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100:2016','ISO 9001:2015','IPC-610 (Operator Certification)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Mixed Technology Assembly", "PCB Assembly", "BGA Placement and Rework", "Fine Pitch Placement (down to 0.0402)", "Rapid Prototyping", "Engineering Design Services", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "Design for Test (DFT)", "Design for Assembly (DFA)", "Turnkey Manufacturing", "Consigned Material Management", "Box Build Assembly", "Statistical Process Control", "Incoming Inspection", "Final Inspection and Test", "Inventory Management", "Distribution Management", "BOM Analysis and Management", "Obsolete Parts Analysis and Alternate Sourcing", "Counterfeit Parts Prevention", "Documentation Package Creation", "UL/CSA Compliance Support", "FDA Regulatory Compliance Support"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Oil & Gas", "Medical Devices", "Bluetooth & GPS Technology", "Water Treatment", "Wastewater Treatment", "Security Devices", "Controllers", "Sensors", "Cleaning Equipment", "Water Irrigation Controllers"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SMT Lines (0.0402 capability, planned 0.0201)", "Semi-Automatic Insertion Equipment", "Automatic Insertion Equipment", "Computer Aided Manufacturing Systems"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume; low-volume high-mix specialty", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 in Colorado Springs -> /, /about", "AS9100:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about, /services", "IPC-610 certified operators -> /about, /services", "SMT lines down to 0.0402, plans for 0.0201 -> /services", "Low and high vo