UPDATE companies SET description='Manar, Inc. (also operating as Tennplasco) is headquartered in Lafayette, Tennessee. Founded in 1974 by Gene Nolen, a pioneer in plastic injection molding, the company has operated for over 45 years. In 2016, it transitioned to 100% employee ownership, empowering its workforce of approximately 330 employee-owners to invest directly in customer success.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding, offering thermoplastic injection molding, gas-assist molding, and scientific molding across horizontal and vertical presses ranging from 55 to 2,300 tons. It operates multiple facilities: one plant certified to ISO 9001 and ISO 13485 with a white room for medical molding, a second plant certified to ISO 13485 and IATF 16949, and two additional plants certified to IATF 16949. Capabilities extend to in-house tool design, seamless tool transfers, prototyping via additive manufacturing/3D printing, automated assembly, and value-added services such as painting, kitting, and packaging. Process validation (IQ, OQ, PQ) supports early-stage projects.

Manar serves a diverse industrial base including medical device, lawn and garden, consumer products, powersports, automotive and transportation, industrial, aerospace, and power and energy sectors.

Founded on Gene Nolen''s vision to advance plastic injection molding, Manar emphasizes domestic manufacturing, maintaining all production in the USA. The employee-ownership model, adopted in 2016, aligns the team''s incentives with customer outcomes, fostering a culture of accountability and long-term partnership.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Thermoplastic injection molding", "Gas-assist injection molding", "Scientific molding", "In-house tool design", "Seamless tool transfers", "Prototyping", "Additive manufacturing/3D printing", "Automated assembly", "Value-added services (painting, kitting, packaging)", "Process validation (IQ, OQ, PQ)", "Third-party sourcing", "Hard-to-mold and engineering-grade materials", "Horizontal injection molding (55-2,300 tons)", "Vertical injection molding (55-2,300 tons)"], "industries": ["Medical Device", "Lawn & Garden", "Consumer", "Powersports", "Automotive & Transportation", "Industrial", "Aerospace", "Power & Energy"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Horizontal and vertical injection molding presses (55-2,300 tons)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned since 2016", "Multiple certified plants (ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949) including white room for medical molding", "Press capacity from 55 to 2,300 tons with horizontal and vertical molding", "In-house tool design and seamless tool transfers", "Scientific molding expertise with process validation (IQ, OQ, PQ)", "Automated assembly and value-added services (painting, kitting, packaging)", "Made in USA commitment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 -> db", "Headquarters Lafayette, Tennessee -> db", "Founder Gene Nolen -> /about", "100% employee-owned since 2016 -> /, /about", "Approximately 330 employee-owners -> /about", "Certifications ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949 -> /, db", "Press ranges 55-2,300 