UPDATE companies SET description='MECA Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1961 in Denville, New Jersey. The privately held corporation operates under the name Microwave Equipment & Components of America and has manufactured RF and microwave components in the United States for over six decades.

The company designs and produces a broad line of passive RF and microwave components, including fixed attenuators, directional couplers, hybrid couplers, isolators, circulators, power dividers and combiners, RF loads, DC blocks, bias tees, cables, and adapters. Its portfolio extends to integrated assemblies and a high-reliability ML series qualified to military specifications such as MIL-DTL-23971, MIL-DTL-15370, MIL-DTL-39030E, and MIL-STD-202. Products cover frequencies up to 50 GHz and are built by J-STD certified assemblers with standard and enhanced screening options.

MECA serves public safety, rail and transportation, commercial wireless (including distributed antenna systems), 5G/6G and VSAT/SATCOM millimeter-wave markets, as well as aerospace, defense, and space programs. Rail products meet EN50155 environmental standards, while low-PIM components address commercial wireless infrastructure with no power derating to 85 °C. The company also provides value-added kitting and integration of customer-supplied parts.

MECA emphasizes rugged, U.S.-made construction backed by a 36-month warranty. Its differentiators include IP67/68-rated enclosures, thermal and electrical screening processes, and a focus on traceability for ground, air, and space communications where qualification requirements are stringent.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF/microwave component design", "Precision machining and assembly (J-STD certified)", "Thermal screening", "Electrical and mechanical verification testing", "Enhanced qualification screening", "Low PIM manufacturing", "High-reliability (ML series) production per MIL specs", "Value-added kitting and integration", "Custom fabrication of customer-supplied parts", "Connectorization (SMA, N, BNC, TNC, 7/16, 4.3/10, 2.92 mm, 2.4 mm)", "Environmental testing (vibration, shock, thermal cycling) per EN50155", "IP67/68 sealing"], "industries": ["Public Safety", "Rail & Transportation", "Commercial Wireless", "5G/6G", "VSAT/SATCOM", "Millimeter-Wave", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Space"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["36-month warranty on all products", "ML series qualified to MIL-DTL-23971, MIL-DTL-15370, MIL-DTL-39030E, and MIL-STD-202", "Standard and enhanced screening (thermal, electrical, mechanical)", "J-STD certified assembly and technician workforce", "Low PIM components with no power derating to 85 \u00b0C"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1961 -> db", "Headquarters Denville, NJ -> db", "Privately held -> /, /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> db, /, /about", "RoHS compliant -> db", "Manufactures RF/microwave components up to 50 GHz -> /, /about", "Product categories (power dividers, couplers, terminations, attenuators, hybrids, adapters, cables, isolators, circulators, DC blocks, bias tees, low PIM, integrated assemblies, MIL-DTL) -> /", "Industries served: public safety, rail & transportation, commercial wireless, 5G/6G, VSAT/SATCOM millim