UPDATE companies SET description='Currier MOS Plastics operates from San Jose, California, with additional facilities in Central New York and Southern California. The company traces its roots to 1982, when Currier Plastics began pursuing a vision of raising service and quality standards in the molding industry.

The company provides turnkey injection molding and blow molding services for Class II and Class III medical devices, running horizontal and vertical injection molding machines inside ISO Class 7 and ISO Class 8 cleanrooms. Capabilities extend to insert molding, two-shot molding, over-molding, and a range of secondary operations including ultrasonic welding, pad and plate printing, cleanroom assembly, kitting, and component preparation. The firm emphasizes end-to-end support from design-for-manufacturing engineering through full-dimensional layout inspection and statistical process control.

Currier MOS Plastics serves medical device, pharmaceutical, drug delivery, diagnostics, life science, and consumer health markets, along with personal care, packaging, consumer products, telecommunications, electronics, and food and beverage sectors. Named customers include Abbott, Agilent, Allergan, and Cepheid, for whom the company produces fluidic components, diagnostic test kits, surgical instruments, implants, syringes, catheters, and electronic device housings.

The company cites its V² philosophy — value multiplied by velocity — as a guiding principle, supported by a continuous improvement program organized into six pillar teams. A sustainability initiative called the 6 Green Program Directions governs material sourcing and waste reduction across its environmentally focused injection and blow molding operations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','FDA registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical injection molding", "Blow molding", "Insert molding", "Two-shot molding", "Over-molding", "Cleanroom manufacturing (ISO Class 7, ISO Class 8)", "Device assembly", "Ultrasonic welding", "Pad printing", "Plate printing", "Cleanroom assembly and kitting", "Component preparation", "Design for manufacturing", "Engineering support", "Full-dimensional layout inspection", "Statistical process control (SPC) testing"], "industries": ["Medical device", "Pharmaceutical", "Drug delivery", "Diagnostics", "Life science", "Consumer health", "Personal care", "Packaging", "Consumer products", "Telecommunications", "Electronics", "Food and beverage"], "materials": ["Medical-grade plastics"], "equipment": ["Horizontal medical injection molding machines", "Vertical medical injection molding machines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485 certified and FDA registered with ISO Class 7 and Class 8 cleanrooms", "Turnkey manufacturing for Class II and Class III medical devices", "Insert molding, two-shot molding, and over-molding capabilities", "In-house assembly, ultrasonic welding, pad and plate printing, cleanroom kitting", "Continuous improvement program structured around six pillar teams"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> /about-us", "Headquarters San Jose, California -> db", "Facilities in Central NY and Southern California -> /", "ISO 13485 certified -> /, /capabilities, db", "FDA registered -> /", "ISO Class 7 and Class 8 cleanrooms -> /, /services, /capabilities", "Horizontal and vertical injection molding machines -> /", "Turnkey Class II and Class III medical device manufacturing -> /, /services", "Insert molding, two-shot molding, over-molding -> /services", "Assembly, ultrasonic welding, pad printing, plate printing, kitting -> /services", "Customers: Abbott, Agilent, Allergan, Cepheid -> /", "Industries served list -> /services, /capabilities", "V\u00b2 philosophy and six pillar teams -> /about-us", "6 Green Program Directions sustainability -> /about-us", "Full-dimensional layout inspection and SPC -> /quality"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mos-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='MP Components Inc. traces its roots to the fall of 1973, when Otto Schlatter and Larry Wiersma founded Model Pattern Company Inc. in Byron Center, Michigan. The shop began as a model and pattern operation, handcrafting prototypes for local manufacturers. In January 1996, the company was renamed MP Components to reflect its expanding capabilities.

The company designs and builds a range of tooling, including checking fixtures (from simple to complex automated units), models and foundry patterns, aluminum vacuum molds, blow molds, foam and compression molds, match-metal trim dies, and special machinery. It also provides computer-aided design (CAD) services, CMM inspection, and CNC machining. Operations span a 28,000-square-foot plant in Michigan and a 10,000-square-foot facility in Tennessee, equipped with current-generation machining and measurement technology.

MP Components serves manufacturers in the automotive, furniture, appliance, aerospace, and medical industries. Its customer base extends across the continental United States, Canada, and Mexico, with the two Midwestern locations positioned for broad geographic coverage.

The founders'' original mission — to deliver handcrafted quality models and prototypes — continues to shape the company''s approach. MP Components emphasizes a one-stop-shop model for tooling needs, backed by ISO 9001 and ISO/IEC 17025 certifications, and highlights rapid turnaround times as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO/IEC 17025']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fixture and gauge design and build", "Model and pattern making", "Mold design and build (aluminum vacuum, blow, foam, compression)", "Match-metal trim die manufacturing", "Special machinery design and build", "Computer-aided design (CAD)", "CMM inspection", "CNC machining", "Checking fixture manufacturing (simple to complex automated)", "Foundry pattern production", "Automated machinery integration", "Engineering services"], "industries": ["automotive", "furniture", "appliance", "aerospace", "medical"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": ["CMM", "CNC"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded fall 1973 by Otto Schlatter and Larry Wiersma as Model Pattern Company Inc. -> /about", "Renamed MP Components in January 1996 -> /about", "Second-generation leadership: Joe Schlatter and John Schlatter -> /about", "Facilities: 28,000 sq ft in Michigan, 10,000 sq ft in Tennessee -> /about", "Capabilities: checking fixtures, models & foundry patterns, aluminum vacuum molds, blow molds, foam and compression molds, automated machinery, trim dies, CAD, CMM, CNC -> /about", "Industries served: automotive, furniture, appliance, aerospace, medical -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 9001 and ISO/IEC 17025 -> /", "Serves continental US, Canada, Mexico -> /", "Rapid turnaround time emphasized -> /", "One-stop shop for tooling needs -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mp-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Masimo Semiconductor was founded in 1982 in Hudson, New Hampshire, and has since focused on the development and manufacture of III‑V opto‑electronic devices.

The company specializes in wafer epitaxy, foundry services, and device fabrication. Its core processes include GaAs and InP MOCVD epitaxy, custom III‑V epitaxial growth, device fabrication, optical coating evaporation, and device testing. Masimo Semiconductor offers prototype through high‑volume production runs, supported by an on‑site Agnitron A300 MOCVD reactor installed in 2023 and advanced metrology equipment for epitaxial film and device characterization.

Masimo Semiconductor serves the healthcare, industrial, energy, datacom/telecom, security, and consumer products markets. Its components are used in high‑brightness LEDs for medical and commercial applications, as well as in optoelectronics, biomedical devices, and telecommunications systems.

The company positions itself as a cost‑effective product development and manufacturing partner that does not compete with its customers. It emphasizes close collaboration, protection of customer intellectual property, fast turnaround from prototype to volume, and a staff of epitaxy professionals with over 35 years of industry experience. Quality management conforms to ISO 9001:2015.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["GaAs/InP MOCVD epitaxy", "Foundry services", "Device fabrication", "Device testing", "Optical coating evaporation", "Custom III\u2011V epitaxial services", "Epitaxial film and device characterization"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Industrial", "Energy", "Datacom/Telecom", "Security", "Consumer Products", "Optoelectronics", "Biomedical", "Commercial Applications"], "materials": ["Gallium Arsenide (GaAs)", "Indium Phosphide (InP)"], "equipment": ["Agnitron A300 MOCVD Reactor"], "volume": "Prototype to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Does not compete with customers; protects customer IP and confidentiality", "Fast turnaround from prototype to high\u2011volume manufacturing", "Experienced epitaxy staff with 35+ years of industry knowledge", "Advanced metrology for epitaxial film and device characterization", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1982 -> db", "Headquarters in Hudson, New Hampshire -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /about-us", "Specializes in wafer epitaxy, foundry services, device fabrication -> /about-us", "GaAs and InP MOCVD epitaxy -> /", "Foundry services -> /", "Device testing -> /", "Optical coating evaporation -> /", "Custom III-V epitaxial services -> /", "Agnitron A300 MOCVD Reactor installed 2023 -> /", "Advanced metrology equipment -> /about-us", "Industries served: healthcare, industrial, energy, datacom/telecom, security, consumer products -> /about-us", "High brightness LEDs for medical, optoelectronics, commercial applications -> /", "Does not compete with customers, protects IP -> /about-us", "Fast turnaround prototype to high volume -> /about-us", "Experienced staff with 35+ years industry knowledge -> /about-us", "Cost-effective product development and manufacturing partner -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='masimo-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Matrix Plastic Products operates from Wood Dale, Illinois, just outside Chicago. The company traces its roots to 1978 when it began as Matrix Tooling with seven employees and a family tradition of moldmaking craftsmanship. By 1994 the business had expanded into injection molding, and by 2000 it was running volume production in a facility that had doubled in size.

Today Matrix provides injection molding, moldmaking, and assembly with a focus on surgical precision. Its capabilities include scientific and decoupled molding processes, multi-shot molding, and micro molding for miniature components. The shop runs three shifts on presses ranging from 20 to 300 tons, employs 140 people, and is expanding from its current Wood Dale location to an 88,000-square-foot facility in nearby Bloomingdale. An ISO Class 8 cleanroom supports medical-grade molding and assembly.

The company serves global leaders in the medical device, electronics, personal care, and safety industries. Typical projects include minimally invasive surgical instruments, micro medical devices, and high-performance electronic components. Customers rely on Matrix for full traceability and device-history records that meet regulatory requirements.

Matrix differentiates itself through nearly five decades of in-house design-for-manufacturability and moldmaking expertise, a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016, and a culture that blends traditional craftsmanship with continuous investment in automation and inspection technology. The firm emphasizes reliability, responsiveness, and direct communication between project teams and customers.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Moldmaking (Class 101 tools)", "Assembly and sub-assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Multi-shot molding", "Micro molding", "Cleanroom molding (ISO Class 8)", "Scientific molding", "Decoupled molding", "Custom manufacturing", "Inspection and metrology (vision, touch probe, laser)", "3D printing", "Flow simulation (SolidWorks Plastics Premium)", "CNC machining", "Tooling design and build"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Electronics", "Personal care", "Safety equipment", "High-performance industrial"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade resins", "Implantable bio-resins", "Commodity-grade polymers"], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses (20\u2013300 tons)", "CNC machining centers", "Machining automation", "Vision inspection systems", "Touch probe inspection", "Laser inspection", "SolidWorks CAD", "SolidWorks Plastics Premium Advanced Flow Simulation", "3D printers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house DFM and moldmaking expertise since 1978", "ISO 8 cleanroom for medical molding and assembly", "Scientific and decoupled molding processes", "Three-shift operation on 20\u2013300 ton presses", "Direct customer access to project teams"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1978 as Matrix Tooling with seven employees -> /about-us", "Expanded into injection molding in 1994 -> /about-us", "Volume production by 2000, facility doubled -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Wood Dale, Illinois -> /about-us, db", "140 employees -> /about-us", "Expanding to 88,000 sq ft facility in Bloomingdale -> /about-us", "Three-shift operation, presses 20-300 tons -> /services", "ISO Class 8 cleanroom for medical molding/assembly -> /, /about-us, /services", "Scientific molding and decoupled molding processes -> /, /services", "Multi-shot molding, micro molding capabilities -> /services", "Industries: medical device, electronics, personal care, safety -> /about-us, /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified since 1999, ISO 13485:2016 since 2010 -> /about-us", "In-house DFM and moldmaking expertise -> /about-us, /services", "CNC technology and machining automation -> /services", "Inspection equipment: vision, touch probe, laser -> /about-us, /services", "SolidWorks and Plastics Premium Advanced Flow Simulation -> /services", "3D printing used in design process -> /services", "Materials: engineering grades, implantable bio-resins, commodity polymers -> /services", "Direct communication with project teams, reliability/responsiveness -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='matrix-plastic-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='McCann Fabrication operates from New Gloucester, Maine, where brothers Bill and Dick McCann founded the company in 1983.

The shop delivers full-service custom metal fabrication across a 26,400-square-foot facility staffed by 30-plus employees running three shifts, seven days a week. Core processes include cutting, bending, welding, machining, 5-axis waterjet cutting, shearing, forming, plasma cutting, plate rolling, punching, band sawing, and finishing, supported by handling and logistics. Key equipment includes Cincinnati hydraulic press brakes (350- and 175-ton), a PaR 5-axis waterjet system with a 73-by-121-inch work envelope, Cincinnati shears, a Vicon CNC plasma cutter, a JetLine seam welder, Hyd-Mech band saws, a Roundo plate roll, and a Geka ironworker.

McCann serves customers in commercial construction, food processing, manufacturing, ornamental metalwork, pharmaceutical, power generation, public works, pulp and paper, and wastewater treatment, among other sectors.

The company emphasizes personalized service enabled by its family ownership, collaborative partnerships with engineering firms and coating houses, and a continuous investment in technology such as 3D CAD (Inventor 2020) and annual equipment upgrades to meet demanding deadlines.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "5-axis waterjet cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Press brake bending", "Shearing", "Plate rolling", "Punching", "Band saw cutting", "Ironworking", "Welding (GTAW, seam)", "Finishing", "Material handling and logistics"], "industries": ["Commercial Construction", "Food Processing", "Manufacturing", "Ornamental", "Pharmaceutical", "Power Generation", "Public Works", "Pulp and Paper", "Waste Water Treatment"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Mild steel"], "equipment": ["350 Ton Cincinnati 12'' Hydraulic Press Brake", "175 Ton Cincinnati 12'' Hydraulic Press Brake", "PaR 5-axis Waterjet Cutting Systems", "Cincinnati 1/2\" x 10'' Hydraulic Shear", "Cincinnati Mod 1810 Power Shear", "Vicon CNC Hypertherm HT2000 Plasma Machine", "JetLine LWS-120 GTAW Combination Seam Welder", "Hyd-Mech S-23A Automatic Band Saws", "Roundo PS250 5/16\" x 10'' Plate Roll", "Geka 70 Ton Iron Worker"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned structure enabling personalized service", "Three-shift, seven-day production schedule for tight deadlines", "5-axis waterjet cutting capacity up to 4-inch stainless steel", "Collaborative partnerships with engineering firms and coating houses", "Ongoing technology upgrades including 3D CAD and annual equipment refresh"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1983 by Bill and Dick McCann -> /about-us", "Family-owned, three generations, 75% workforce 15+ years -> /about-us", "26,400 sq ft facility, 30+ employees, three shifts 7 days -> /, /services", "Processes: cutting, bending, welding, machining, waterjet, shearing, forming, plasma, plate rolling, punching, band saw, finishing, lo