UPDATE companies SET description='Mega Electronics Inc. operates from New Brunswick, New Jersey. Founded in 1984, the company began with the goal of supplying a single source for components that deliver power from the wall into electronic products for any global location.

The company designs, manufactures, and distributes power cords, power supplies, and DC/DC converters. Its power supply line spans wall-mount, desktop, DIN-rail, and open-frame formats from 5 W to 960 W, carrying UL, CSA, CE, CCC, CB, and other global safety marks. DC/DC converters range from 0.25 W to 200 W in through-hole, surface-mount, and chassis-mount packages. Mega also produces IEC Lock locking connectors, EN60309 industrial plugs, anti-microbial cables, twist-lock extension cords up to 30 A, and card-edge connectors that mate directly to printed circuit boards. An ISO 9001-certified production facility supports these lines, and a U.S. warehouse enables stock shipment worldwide. The firm offers vendor-managed inventory (VMI), just-in-time (JIT), and kanban programs for blanket and stock-and-release orders.

Mega serves commercial and industrial markets including medical equipment, data centers, computer peripherals, food-service machinery, industrial equipment, networking hardware, and vending machines. Its power cords hold approvals for North America, Europe, Asia, Australia, South America, and the Middle East, allowing customers to ship products globally without separate cord qualifications.

The company cites three pillars—high-quality products, excellent customer service, and superior product knowledge—as its foundation. It emphasizes single-stop shopping for power components, worldwide approval expertise, dedicated engineering support from concept through product life cycle, and a stock-based fulfillment model backed by VMI, JIT, and kanban services.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Power supply design and manufacturing (wall mount, desktop, DIN rail, open frame)", "Power cord manufacturing and assembly (international, North American, hospital grade)", "DC/DC converter design and manufacturing (through-hole, SMD, chassis mount)", "IEC Lock connector manufacturing", "EN60309 industrial plug and connector manufacturing", "Anti-microbial cable production", "Twist-lock extension cord manufacturing (up to 30 A, 600 V)", "Card-edge connector manufacturing for direct PCB power connection", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI) services", "Just-in-Time (JIT) delivery services", "Kanban inventory management", "Global compliance and approvals management", "Engineering support from concept to product release", "Product life cycle support", "Blanket order and stock-and-release fulfillment"], "industries": ["Medical", "Data Centers", "Computer Peripherals", "Food Service", "Industrial Equipment", "Networking Equipment", "Vending Machines", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001 certified production facility", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI), JIT, and kanban programs", "Global approvals on power cords for worldwide shipment from stock", "Power supplies from 5 W to 960 W with multiple international safety certifications", "Patented IEC Lock locking connectors and card-edge PCB power connectors"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in New Brunswick, New Jersey -> db, /about", "Founded in 1984 -> db, homepage ''Since 1984''", "Founded to provide single source for power components -> description, /about", "Designs, manufactures, distributes power cords, power supplies, DC/DC converters -> /about", "Power supplies 5W-960W with UL, CSA, CE, CCC, CB, etc. -> /about", "DC/DC converters 0.25W-200W through-hole, SMD, chassis mount -> /about", "IEC Lock locking connectors, EN60309 plugs, anti-microbial cables, twist-lock extension cords, card-edge connectors -> homepage, /about", "ISO 9001 certified production facility -> /about", "U.S. warehouse, stock shipment worldwide -> /about", "VMI, JIT, kanban programs -> /about, homepage", "Markets served: Medical, Data Centers, Computer Peripherals, Food Service, Industrial Equipment, Networking Equipment, Vending Machines -> homepage", "Global power cord approvals for worldwide shipping -> /about", "Three pillars: high-quality products, excellent customer service, superior product knowledge -> /about", "Single-stop shopping, worldwide approval expertise, engineering support, stock-based fulfillment -> /about, homepage", "ROHS compliance -> certifications array", "No founders named, ownership not disclosed -> db, /about", "No employee count, facility size, volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> all sources"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mega-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Melink Solar, headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio, traces its roots to 1987 when engineer and entrepreneur Steve Melink founded Melink Corporation as an HVAC testing and balancing firm. Melink''s invention of the Intelli-Hood variable-speed control system for commercial kitchen ventilation became an industry standard, establishing the company''s focus on energy efficiency.

In 2008, the company launched its solar division, Melink Solar, as a full-service commercial EPC (Engineering, Procurement, Construction) provider delivering turnkey projects that encompass system design and engineering, material procurement, construction, and operations and maintenance. The firm has installed more than 275 megawatts and 650,000 panels across the United States, ranging from small commercial rooftops to a 15‑megawatt utility-scale array in Piqua, Ohio, and it owns and operates 10 megawatts of solar capacity.

Melink Solar serves independent power producers, utilities, commercial and industrial facilities, schools and universities, religious organizations, municipalities, government agencies, and non‑profits. Notable clients include the Cincinnati Zoo & Botanical Garden, and the parent corporation has worked with brands such as Apple, Google, Walmart, and Disney.

The company''s differentiation stems from its demonstrated commitment to sustainability: its Cincinnati headquarters achieved LEED Platinum and Net Zero Energy status in 2010, among the first 25 buildings worldwide to do so, and Melink Solar tests solar technologies on its own campus before deploying them for customers.', certifications=ARRAY['LEED Platinum','LEED Gold','Energy Star']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["System Design & Engineering", "Material Procurement", "Construction", "Operations & Maintenance", "Ground Mount Installation", "Roof Mount Installation", "Solar Canopy Installation", "Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) Development", "Financial Analysis", "Permitting & Interconnection", "Customer Training & Monitoring", "Solar Module Recyclability Assessment"], "industries": ["Independent Power Producers", "Utilities", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Education (Schools & Universities)", "Religious Organizations", "Municipalities", "Government", "Non-Profits"], "materials": ["Monocrystalline silicon", "Polycrystalline silicon", "Flexible solar panels", "Tier 1 solar modules", "Silicon", "Glass", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Intelli-Hood variable-speed control systems", "Tier 1 solar modules", "Inverters"], "volume": "Up to 15 MW per project; 275+ MW cumulative installed", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service EPC delivering turnkey solar projects", "Owns and operates 10 MW of solar arrays, proving performance firsthand", "Headquarters is LEED Platinum and Net Zero Energy certified (2010)", "275+ MW installed across the U.S. since 2008", "35+ years of energy-efficiency experience dating to 1987"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1987 by Steve Melink -> /about", "Started as HVAC testing and balancing firm -> /about", "Invented Intelli-Hood variable-speed control systems -> /about", "Launched solar division in 2008 -> /about", "Full-service commercial solar EPC -> /", "Services: System Design & Engineering, Material Procurement, Construction, Operations & Maintenance -> /", "Installed 275+ MW and 650,000+ panels across U.S. -> /", "Owns and operates 10 MW of solar arrays -> /about", "First 15 MW utility-scale project in Piqua, Ohio (2019) -> /about", "Headquarters LEED Platinum and Net Zero Energy (2010) -> /about", "Serves: Independent Power Producers, Utilities, Commercial, Industrial, Schools, Universities, Religious Organizations, Municipalities, Government, Non-Profits -> /", "Client example: Cincinnati Zoo & Botanical Garden -> /", "Parent corporation works with Apple, Google, Walmart, Disney -> /about", "Tests solar technologies on own campus -> /", "Uses Tier 1 solar modules with silicon cells -> /", "Offers Power Purchase Agreements (PPAs) -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='melink-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Metal Works Corporation was incorporated in 1956 in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. The company has operated for more than 65 years as a specialty metal fabrication and manufacturing firm.

The company operates an in-house machine shop producing specialty springs from wire diameters of 0.002 to 2 inches across all alloys, custom rotating mechanical seals, and various industrial components. Its capabilities span pipe and tube bending, coiling, welding, general fabrication, and custom coil design.

Metal Works serves industrial customers requiring fabricated metal components, springs, and seals. The company describes itself as customer-oriented but does not list specific industries or named clients in its public materials.

