UPDATE companies SET description='Micron Corporation has operated from Norwood, Massachusetts since 1982. Founded as a small shop serving local OEMs with precision electronics manufacturing, the company remains family owned and operated, with decisions made close to the shop floor and a focus on long-term customer relationships.

Today Micron provides electronic manufacturing services spanning SMT assembly (including fine-pitch, QFN/BGA, and 01005 placement on a MYCRONIC MY300 line), through-hole and mixed-technology assembly, box build and electromechanical integration, cable and harness assembly, conformal coating and potting, selective soldering, and rework to IPC standards. The shop supports prototypes, new product introductions, and recurring high-mix, low-volume production runs, with inspection capabilities that include 3D AOI and X-ray verification for hidden solder joints. Workmanship follows IPC-A-610 and J-STD-001 Class 2 or 3 as specified.

The company serves OEMs in medical and life sciences, aerospace and defense (ITAR-registered), energy and cleantech, automotive aftermarket, industrial automation, and research and development. Micron also manufactures its own consumer products, the RODAR® II ultrasonic pest repeller and EnergAire® ionizer air purifier, leveraging the same EMS expertise.

Micron emphasizes responsive communication, high-mix flexibility, and a partnership mindset that aims to act as an extension of the customer''s team. The family ownership structure enables direct access to project managers and quick decision-making, while documented quality practices, traceability, and supply chain support (turnkey, consignment, or hybrid) help reduce risk on complex assemblies.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','RoHS/REACH Compliant','BBB Accredited Business']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT Assembly (fine-pitch, QFN/BGA, 01005, profile-tuned reflow)", "Through Hole Assembly (hand solder, wave solder)", "Mixed-Technology Assembly", "Box Build & Integration", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Cable & Harness Assembly", "Prototypes & NPI (DFM review, pilot builds, production handoff)", "Functional Test & Programming", "Firmware Loading", "Conformal Coating & Potting", "Selective Soldering", "Rework & Repair to IPC standards", "3D AOI Inspection", "X-ray Inspection (BGA, QFN, hidden joints)", "BOM Review & Component Sourcing", "Alternate Part Review", "Turnkey Procurement", "Consignment Inventory Management", "First Article Inspection", "Traceability & Documentation Control", "IPC-A-610/J-STD-001 Class 2/3 Workmanship", "ITAR Compliant Manufacturing", "RoHS/REACH Compliance"], "industries": ["Medical & Life Sciences", "Aerospace & Defense", "Energy & CleanTech", "Automotive Aftermarket", "Industrial & Automation", "Research & Development", "Consumer Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["MYCRONIC MY300"], "volume": "Prototype to recurring production (high-mix, low-volume)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated with decisions made close to the shop floor", "High-mix, low-volume flexibility with responsive problem-solving", "Direct access to project managers and a local New England team", "IPC-A-610/J-STD-001 Class 2/3 workmanship with 3D AOI and X-ray verification", "Turnkey, consignment, or hybrid build mod