UPDATE companies SET description='Midcon Cables Company was founded in 1972 in North Myrtle Beach, South Carolina. The business is employee-owned and operates facilities in both Missouri and South Carolina.

The company manufactures custom and build-to-print cable assemblies, harnesses, and molded interconnects for demanding applications. Its capabilities include cold molding and over-molding per MIL-M-24041, RF coaxial connector and cable assembly termination, fiber optic cable assemblies (single- and multi-mode), and proprietary organized-wiring technologies such as EverFlex and MicroFlex. Engineering design support, qualification testing, and full documentation are provided alongside prototyping and full-rate production.

Midcon serves the aerospace and defense, industrial, and medical markets. Its products are used on aircraft, ground vehicles, missiles, unmanned systems, rotorcraft, ships, and communications platforms. The company also supports commercial customers with value-added wiring solutions.

Midcon differentiates itself with its EverFlex organized-wiring system, which replaces conventional harnesses and flex circuits with a low-profile, robust alternative that integrates controlled circuit positions and tie-downs. A proprietary quick-set potting compound reduces molding cycle times, and the MicroFlex process uses NC machining to produce ultra-flat ribbon assemblies that can incorporate power, signal, RF, and fiber optic lines.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','NADCAP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Build-to-print cable assembly", "Potting and molding (cold molding, over-molding per MIL-M-24041)", "Rugged cable assembly", "EverFlex organized wiring", "MicroFlex flat ribbon assembly", "Custom organized wiring design", "RF coaxial connector and cable assembly termination", "Banding adapter fabrication", "Fiber optic cable assembly (single- and multi-mode)", "Engineering design support", "Qualification testing and documentation", "Prototyping and full-rate production"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Industrial", "Medical", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to high volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary quick-set potting compound reduces molding cycle time", "EverFlex organized-wiring system replaces conventional harnesses and flex circuits", "MicroFlex NC-machined flat ribbon assemblies integrate power, signal, RF, and fiber", "AS9100 and NADCAP certified quality system", "Employee-owned with facilities in Missouri and South Carolina"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1972 -> db", "Headquarters in North Myrtle Beach, South Carolina -> db", "Employee-owned -> /about", "Facilities in Missouri and South Carolina -> /about", "AS9100 and NADCAP certified -> /about", "Build-to-print cable assemblies and harnesses -> /", "EverFlex organized wiring technology -> /", "MicroFlex NC-machined flat ribbon assemblies -> /", "Custom organized wiring design -> /", "RF coaxial connector and cable assembly termination -> /", "Banding adapters for shield termination -> /", "Cold molding and over-molding per MIL-M-24041 -> /", "Proprietary quick-set potting compound -> /", "Fiber optic cable assemblies (single- and multi-mode) -> /", "Engineering design support and qualification testing -> /", "Serves aerospace & defense, industrial, medical, commercial markets -> /, /about", "Products used on aircraft, ground vehicles, missiles, unmanned systems, rotorcraft, ships, communications -> /", "Preferred supplier recognition -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='midcon-cables-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Millennium Circuits Limited (MCL) is a printed circuit board supplier headquartered in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania. Founded in 2005, the company has focused exclusively on bare PCB procurement, positioning itself as a value-added partner for customers ranging from prototype to production volumes.

MCL supplies bare PCBs across a wide range of technologies: rigid, flex, rigid-flex, aluminum, ceramic, heavy copper, RF/microwave, and HDI constructions. Its manufacturing network—both domestic and offshore—supports 1 to 44 layers, a 35:1 drill aspect ratio, maximum panel sizes of 24 by 51 inches, blind and buried vias, micro vias, via-in-pad with conductive or non-conductive fill, controlled impedance, and high copper thicknesses. Surface finish options include ENIG, immersion silver, immersion tin, ENEPIG, HASL, lead-free HAL, OSP, hard gold, soft gold, and selective finishes. The company also provides engineering services such as design-for-manufacturability reviews, design rule checks, stack-up design, impedance modeling, panelization, and cost consulting, along with product life cycle management. MCL reports 1,106 customers served, a 97% on-time delivery rate, and 99.6% of PCBs shipped without defects, backed by over 100 years of combined PCB manufacturing expertise among its team.

The company serves industries including medical, automotive, power and energy, industrial equipment, telecommunications, defense, consumer electronics, marine, test and measurement, and LED lighting. Its customer base comprises contract manufacturers, original equipment manufacturers, and design firms.

MCL differentiates itself through a U.S.-based Customer Concierge team that provides same-day quotes and dedicated support from request through delivery. It maintains strategic, long-term partnerships with vetted manufacturing facilities—selected via a proprietary Vendor IQ evaluation—rather than sourcing from the lowest bidder. The company is ISO 9001 certified (since 2014) and complies with RoHS, REACH, ITAR, IPC-A-600, and IPC-6012 standards, emphasizing a ''right-fit'' supplier approach to ensure quality and consistency.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','RoHS','REACH','ITAR','IPC-A-600','IPC-6012']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Bare PCB supply", "Quick-turn prototypes", "Production quantities", "Rigid PCBs", "Flex PCBs", "Rigid-flex PCBs", "Aluminum PCBs", "Ceramic PCBs", "Heavy copper PCBs", "RF/microwave PCBs", "HDI PCBs", "1-44 layer fabrication", "35:1 drill aspect ratio", "Blind/buried vias", "Micro vias", "Via-in-pad (conductive, non-conductive, copper plug)", "Controlled impedance", "High copper thickness", "Surface finishes: ENIG, immersion silver, immersion tin, ENEPIG, HASL, Pb-free HAL, OSP, hard gold, soft gold, selective finishes", "Engineering services: DFM, DRC, stack-up design, impedance modeling, panelization, cost consulting", "Product life cycle management", "Supplier management (Vendor IQ)", "Domestic and offshore manufacturing coordination"], "industries": ["Medical", "Automotive", "Power & Energy", "Industrial Equipment", "Telecommunications", "Defense", "Consumer Electronics", "Marine", "Test & Measurement", "LED Lighting"], "materials": ["FR4", "Aluminum", "Ceramic", "Heavy Copper", "RF/Microwave Substrates", "High-Speed Digital Materials", "High-Frequency RF Materials", "High-Temperature Materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production quantities", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day quotes and rapid quote response", "U.S.-based Customer Concierge team for end-to-end support", "Strategic dome