UPDATE companies SET description='Mission Plastics Inc. (MPI) was founded in 1982 in Ontario, California, as a custom injection-molding operation. The company is now headquartered in Nashville, Arkansas, and operates additional facilities in Rancho Cucamonga, California, and Mexicali, Mexico. President Robert Guy leads the organization, which has grown into a full-spectrum manufacturer serving medical, automotive, and commercial sectors.

The company provides precision injection molding, overmolding, insert molding, thin-wall molding, and multi-cavity family molding, supported by in-house tool design, mold making, and automation. Secondary services include plastics and metal CNC machining, assembly, and a full metrology lab with CMM and Keyence laser scanning. The Rancho Cucamonga site houses an on-site tool room and metrology lab, while the Mexicali plant runs 40 molding machines ranging from 55 to 400 tons, with press capacity from 7 to 720 tons and a Class 8 clean room for 7–310-ton presses. Both sites operate 24/7 and handle prototype through high-volume production.

Mission Plastics serves medical device OEMs, automotive suppliers, and commercial product manufacturers. Medical customers have included CareFusion/BD (AirLife respiratory consumables), Safety Syringe (a Beckton Dickinson company), and Parker/Legris. Commercial work spans consumer components, electrical enclosures, and irrigation fittings, with Taral Plastic Container Company cited as a long-term partner.

The company emphasizes scientific molding methodologies, including process capability studies via Minitab, design of experiments, and RJG Master Molder expertise. Its quality system is certified to ISO 13485 for medical devices and ISO 9001, with validation capabilities covering IQ/OQ/PQ and PPAP. A nearshore supply chain model, combining U.S. engineering with Mexican production, is positioned to reduce lead times and logistics risk.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Overmolding & Insert Molding", "Thin-Wall Molding", "Multi-Cavity & Family Molding", "Assembly & Post-Molding Operations", "Plastics & Metal CNC Machining", "Full Metrology (CMM & Keyence Laser)", "Non-Contact Measurement", "Process Capability Studies (Minitab)", "Design of Experiments (DOE)", "Gauge R&R", "Validation (IQ/OQ/PQ)", "PPAP", "Engineering & Design (DFM/DFMA)", "3D Printing & Test Molding", "Tooling & Prototyping", "Concept & Process Design", "Project Onboarding", "Fulfillment & Logistics", "In-House Automation", "Mold Design & Tooling", "Lean Manufacturing", "Rheology Study", "Cavity Balance & Gate Seal Study"], "industries": ["Medical", "Automotive", "Commercial", "Life Sciences"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["7\u2013720 ton injection molding presses", "7\u2013310 ton presses under ISO Class 8 clean room", "40 molding machines (55\u2013400 ton) at Mexicali facility", "Keyence LM-X Series laser measurement systems", "Coordinate Measuring Machines (CMM)", "All-electric molding machines (transitioning)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 production at both U.S. and Mexico facilities", "Nearshore manufacturing with U.S. engineering and Mexican production", "ISO 13485 certified for medical device molding", "In-house tool design, mold making, and automation integration", "Scientific molding with RJG Master Molder and Minitab process studies"], "facts_used": ["Founded in Ontario, CA, in 1982 -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Headquartered in Nashville, Arkansas -> db", "Facilities in Rancho Cucamonga, CA and Mexicali, Mexico -> / (homepage)", "President Robert Guy -> / (homepage)", "ISO 13485 and ISO 9001 certified -> / (homepage), /quality, db", "Press tonnage 7\u2013720 tons, clean room 7\u2013310 tons Class 8 -> / (homepage)", "Mexicali: 40 machines 55\u2013400 tons, transitioning to all-electric -> /about-us", "24/7 operation -> / (homepage)", "Industries: Medical, Automotive, Commercial -> / (homepage), /about-us", "Medical customers: CareFusion/BD, Safety Syringe, Parker/Legris -> / (homepage) testimonials", "Commercial customer: Taral Plastic Container Company -> / (homepage) testimonials", "Scientific molding, Minitab, RJG Master Molder -> /quality", "Validation capabilities IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP -> /quality", "In-house tool room, metrology lab, automation -> / (homepage)", "Nearshore supply chain reliability -> / (homepage)"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mission-plastics-of-ar-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Modern Welding Company of Kentucky, Inc. operates from Elizabethtown, Kentucky, tracing its roots to June 1932 when John G. Barnard — known as “Mr. Pete” — opened a small job shop in Owensboro. The family-owned business expanded steadily, acquiring plants across the Midwest and South, and by 2022 marked 90 years of continuous operation.

The company manufactures underground and aboveground steel storage tanks, ASME-code pressure vessels, and LPG tanks for flammable and combustible liquids and gases. Its Elizabethtown facility specializes in custom plate work, chute fabrication, wear products, and structural steel fabrication. Modern Welding runs ten tank and vessel fabrication subsidiaries nationwide, two dedicated structural steel plants, and four welding supply stores in Kentucky and Indiana, all linked by a shared information network.

Customers span energy, construction, distillery, agriculture, defense, mining, chemical processing, and petroleum storage. Documented projects include a refinery deisohexanizer tower, UL-142 emergency fuel tanks installed within a hospital footprint, high-capacity fuel storage for a global agribusiness, and bulk propane tanks for poultry facility heating.

Modern Welding positions itself as the largest U.S. supplier of UL-listed steel storage tanks. Its quality program encompasses ASME, NBIC, AWS, AISC, UL, STI, and API standards, and the Elizabethtown plant holds AISC Certified Fabricator status. The company emphasizes domestic production, a regional subsidiary model for faster delivery, and a guaranteed 24-hour quote turnaround.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME','NBIC','AWS','AISC','UL','STI','API','UL-142','AISC Certified Fabricator']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Underground steel storage tank manufacturing", "Aboveground steel storage tank manufacturing", "ASME pressure vessel fabrication", "LPG tank fabrication", "Structural steel fabrication", "Custom plate fabrication", "Chute work fabrication", "Wear product fabrication", "Custom steel fabrication", "Steel sales and services", "Quality assurance per ASME, NBIC, AWS, AISC, UL, STI, API"], "industries": ["Energy", "Construction", "Distillery", "Agriculture", "Defense", "Mining", "Chemical processing", "Petroleum storage", "Healthcare", "Agribusiness", "Poultry farming"], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded June 1932 by John G. Barnard -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "Started as small job shop in Owensboro, Kentucky -> /about", "10 steel tank and vessel fabrication subsidiaries nationwide -> /about", "2 structural steel and custom fabrication facilities -> /about", "4 welding supply stores in Kentucky and Indiana -> /about", "Largest supplier of UL-listed underground and aboveground steel storage tanks -> /about", "Manufactures chemical storage tanks, ASME pressure vessels, structural steel fabrication -> /about", "Products shipped worldwide, 11 subsidiaries linked by information network -> /about", "Elizabethtown plant specializes in custom plate and chute work, wear products, structural steel fabrication -> /", "Serves energy, construction, distillery, agriculture, defense, mining industries -> /", "Quality program includes ASME, NBIC, AWS, AISC, UL, STI, API -> /", "AISC Certified Fabricator -> /", "Made in USA -> /", "Quote response within 24 hours guaranteed -> /", "90th birthday celebrated in 2022 -> /about", "Aboveground tanks: atmospheric tanks for noncorrosive, stable, flammable/combustible liquids, max working pressure 0.5 psig, API tanks up to 15 psig -> /", "Underground tanks: Glasteel II double wall tank for biofuels/additives -> /", "Pressure vessels: ASME pressure vessels and LPG tanks for gases/liquids at high pressures -> /", "Structural & custom fabrication: 85+ years experience -> /", "Project examples: Refinery Deisohexanizer Tower, UL-142 Emergency Fuel Storage for hospital, High-Capacity Fuel Storage for Global Agribusiness, Bulk Propane Storage for Poultry Facility -> /", "Certifications: ASME (from db) -> db", "Headquarters: Elizabethtown, Kentucky -> db", "Founded year: 1932 -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='modern-welding-company-of-kentucky' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Monarch Metal Manufacturing operates from a facility in Denver, Colorado. The company was founded in 2007 with the stated goal of providing reasonably priced, high-quality metal products while keeping manufacturing in the United States.

The shop delivers precision fabrication, precision machining, hardware insertion, and mechanical assembly, managing the full manufacturing sequence from programming through final assembly. Stamping work is outsourced. The 60-person team works in a Denver facility that supports prototype through production runs, positioning the company as a single-source provider for metal components.

The company emphasizes a team-based approach and open communication on production status, aiming to build partnerships that take products from print to finished part with minimal disruption.

Differentiators cited by the company include an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system, advanced scheduling and stocking programs to meet lead-time requirements, and a commitment to domestic manufacturing. The quality policy stresses continuous improvement and adherence to procedures on every job.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision fabrication", "Precision machining", "Hardware insertion", "Mechanical assembly", "Stamping (outsourced)", "CNC programming", "Full manufacturing process management", "Quality management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production", "lead_time": "Reasonable lead times supported by advanced scheduling and stocking programs", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source manufacturing from programming through assembly", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Advanced scheduling and stocking programs for lead-time control", "Commitment to U.S.-based manufacturing", "Open communication policy on production times and processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 in Denver, Colorado -> db, /", "60 employees -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> db, /", "Precision fabrication, machining, hardware insertion, mechanical assembly capabilities -> capabilities (db), /", "Stamping outsourced -> capabilities (db)", "Full manufacturing process from programming to assembly -> products (db), /", "Facility at 550 W 53rd Place, Denver, CO 80216 -> /", "Commitment to keeping manufacturing in America -> description, /", "Team approach, open communication -> /", "Advanced scheduling systems and stocking programs -> /", "Single source for manufacturing -> /", "Quality policy continuous improvement -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='monarch-metal-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Montana Global Health was formed in 2019 as a privately-owned dietary supplement contract manufacturer in Kalispell, Montana. The company was established to serve brand owners seeking custom supplement manufacturing with a focus on quality and accessibility.

The company specializes in multiple delivery formats including capsules, daily dose packs, sachets, stick packs, liquids, powders, and pet supplements. Its capabilities include high-speed encapsulation and state-of-the-art packaging. Specific facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not disclosed.

Montana Global Health serves the dietary supplement and pet supplement industries, working with brand owners of all sizes from startups to large companies. The company emphasizes lower minimum order quantities to accommodate smaller businesses.

